\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar takes a breather, pound gains ahead of BOE meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2022\par 05:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Tom Westbrook and Ankur Banerjee\par        SINGAPORE, Nov 3 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar eased\par slightly on Thursday as investors digested the possibility that\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise interest rates further than expected,\par while sterling edged higher ahead of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  policy\par meeting.    \par     The Fed on Wednesday raised its benchmark funds rate by 75\par basis points (bps) to 3.75-4% as widely expected. The dollar\par initially fell on hints in the Fed's statement of smaller hikes\par ahead, but regained strength after Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2  said that\par the battle against inflation will require borrowing costs to\par rise further.\par     "Incoming data since our last meeting suggests that the\par ultimate level of interest rates will be higher than previously\par expected," Powell told reporters, adding: "It is very premature\par to be thinking about pausing... we have a ways to go."\par     The hawkish stance from Powell dashed hopes of a pivot to a\par less aggressive stance and saw the dollar hit a week-high of\par $0.9810 per euro in early Asia trade. But the\par greenback lost some steam through the day and was last trading\par at $0.983.\par     "We are seeing a slight pullback in dollar after the big\par moves yesterday," Alvin Tan, head of Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy, \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC\par Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2 , pointing out that market activity was muted as\par a result of a public holiday in Japan.     \par     Tan said for the Fed bringing down inflation is more\par important than supporting economic growth and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par will keep on tightening. \par     "They are going to reduce the pace but keep on tightening," \par   he added, noting that this was not something new but pushes\par back the growing narrative of a Fed pivot because of slowdown in\par growth. \par     The U.S. dollar index fell 0.214% at 111.880, coming\par off a session high of 112.19, its highest in seven sessions. \par     The slight retreat in dollar is unlikely to last long. \par     "Strong hawkish messaging from the Fed chair pours cold\par water on premature dovish pivot expectations," said analysts at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citi\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who recommend staying long the U.S. dollar in Asia.\par     "This shall further embolden expectations of policy\par divergence with a much hawkish Fed relative to other central\par banks around the world. Further tightening of financial\par conditions shall put downward pressure on risk assets and\par strengthen the dollar."\par     Meanwhile, the pound was last trading at $1.1412,\par up 0.20% on the day ahead of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  meeting, when\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is on track to raise interest rates by three\par quarters of a percentage point to 3%, its biggest rate rise\par since 1989.\par     "The risk is that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BoE\f28 \uc2 \f2  maintains the current pace of\par tightening and delivers a 50 bps hike," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank\par of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  analyst \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kim Mundy\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "A 50 bps hike would be\par considered 'dovish' by market participants and can push sterling\par lower."\par     Japan's yen remained notably firm and has held at\par 147.24 per dollar as traders continue to watch for any more \par official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent a record $42.8 billion propping up the yen last\par month via a series of unannounced yen purchases, on top of\par almost $20 billion spent in September. \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0442 GMT\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct     High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                 \par                                               Session                                           \par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9829        $0.9816     +0.13%         -13.55%     +0.9839     +0.9810\par  Dollar/Yen                   147.3100       147.7600    -0.31%         +28.06%     +147.9900   +147.2950\par  Euro/Yen         <EURJPY=EB  144.79         145.23      -0.30%         +11.11%     +145.3500   +144.6800\par                   S>                                                                            \par  Dollar/Swiss                 1.0018         1.0032      -0.12%         +9.85%      +1.0040     +1.0006\par  Sterling/Dollar              1.1410         1.1390      +0.21%         -15.61%     +1.1421     +1.1377\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.3687         1.3715      -0.20%         +8.26%      +1.3724     +1.3683\par  Aussie/Dollar                0.6365         0.6348      +0.25%         -12.45%     +0.6372     +0.6325\par  NZ                           0.5832         0.5819      +0.28%         -14.75%     +0.5838     +0.5799\par  Dollar/Dollar                                                                                  \par                                                                                                 \par  All spots\par Tokyo spots\par Europe spots \par Volatilities \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par     \par  (Reporting by Tom Westbrook and Ankur Banerjee; Editing by Shri\par Navaratnam and Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-11-3T05:55:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221103eib300mop\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
