\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Loses Steam Ahead of Rate Decision -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2022\par 14:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0931 ET - The dollar weakens against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the DXY index is down 0.3%, as investors expect the Fed to indicate it is about to reduce the pace of rate increases. "The focus is not so much on the 75 bp rate hike, but on its forward guidance," Bannockburn's \uc2 Marc Chandler\uc2  says in a report. He adds that "we are not convinced that it will go beyond indicating that 50 bp or 75 bp will be debated in December, depending on the data." Chandler also points to speculation that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame volatility. The yen rises 0.8 to the dollar. (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 0930 ET - The eurozone manufacturing purchasing managers index fell to 46.4 in October, this being the weakest print since the heyday of the Covid-19 recession, Oxford Economics' senior economist Mateusz Urban says in a note. "Sharply falling demand remains a key drag, as inflation keeps creeping up and uncertainty is high," the economist says. Although the reduction of backlogs served as a cushion to current output and employment, a deterioration in the coming months is imminent, Oxford Economics forecasts. The expectations for the next 12 months remain bleak, with most producers expecting falls in output, Urban notes. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0915 ET - Bitcoin appears to be in "wait-and-see" mode ahead of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  's policy decision later Wednesday, Oanda says. "It continues to hover around $20,000 and wait for the possibility of some news that could propel it in either direction," Oanda analyst \uc2 Craig Erlam\uc2  says in a note. Time will tell if the Fed provides that today but it doesn't take much for traders to react, he says. Even the slightest hints about the future path of interest rates would trigger a decent move in bitcoin, he says. Bitcoin falls 0.7% to $20,396, according to CoinDesk. The Fed's decision is at 1800 GMT. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0911 ET - Germany's labor market data were once again more resilient than economists expected in October, but might conceal a significant underlying deterioration, \uc2 Citi\uc2  's economists say in a note. Jobless claims increased by 8,000 in October, less than expected, this being the smallest monthly increase since May, when the wave of refugees from Ukraine started boosting unemployment, \uc2 Citi\uc2  says. However, underemployment rose, hiring intentions fell and vacancies dropped, \uc2 Citi\uc2  's economists note. The economic slowdown due to the energy crisis seems to be leaving a mark and \uc2 Citi\uc2  expects this to lead unemployment above 6% in 2023. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0906 ET - The \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  's gilt-sale \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which began on November 1, is likely to lead to a lower peak for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key rate as gilt-market trading returns to normal, says BMO European head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy \uc2 Stephen Gallo\uc2  in a note. After the recent gilt-market crisis, BOE policymakers now have a clear view of gilt-market liquidity functioning and may be more aware of potential systemic risks, which should enable an "orderly" gilt sale \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he says. "We now see Bank rate peaking at 3.75% early next year from our earlier forecast of 4.25%." (miriam.mukuru@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0852 ET - The Swedish krona stands to benefit if the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  boosts risk appetite by failing to take a more "hawkish" than expected stance at Wednesday's meeting that favors continued aggressive policy tightening, \uc2 Saxo Bank\uc2  says. "With the SEK traditionally one of the most sensitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sentiment, a USD sell-off and further rally in risk sentiment could be felt particularly strongly in the USD/SEK exchange rate," \uc2 Saxo Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist \uc2 John Hardy\uc2  says in a note. USD/SEK rises 0.1% to 11.0290. The Fed's interest rate decision is at 1800 GMT. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 ET - Treasury yields get a boost from higher-than-expectect job creation in October's ADP report, but the 10-year stays below Tuesday's level, at 4.045%. The two-year is at 4.541%. The two benchmarks have traded within a range indicating investors expect the Fed to stop hiking when rates reach 4.5% or so. That includes a 75-basis point increase today, while investors are likely to scrutinize the Fed's communication for clues of what is next. The \uc2 CME\uc2  's FedWatch tool gives nearly 50% odds of either a 50 bp or a 25 bp hike in December. Friday's nonfarm payrolls report is likely to have an impact on those odds. (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 0823 ET - Short-sellers could build bets against the Czech koruna ahead of the \uc2 Czech National Bank\uc2  's meeting Thursday given speculation of an end or change to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, ING says. \uc2 CNB\uc2  meetings traditionally attract short positioning in the koruna, which could take EUR/CZK to a range of 24.60-24.70, from 24.5081 currently, ING analyst Frantisek Taborsky says in a note. "Moreover, with the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  's meeting today, we expect pressure on the Central and Eastern Europe [market] to increase during the day, which may lead to a painful end to the current rally in the region." (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0812 ET - \uc2 Yum Brands\uc2  reports its 3Q earnings were unfavorably impacted by foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  translation, the latest fast-food chain to experience a drop in the value of its sales abroad due to the strong US dollar. Yum said foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurt its 3Q earnings by 10 cents per share, and decreased operating profit by $39M. Profits at the parent of \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  , \uc2 KFC\uc2  and Pizza Hut missed expectations, but revenue and same-store sales rose above analyst estimates. Yum reported an adjusted EPS of $1.09 per share, and sales of $1.64B. Shares rise 1% in pre-market trading. (heather.haddon@wsj.com; @heatherhaddon)\par \par \uc2 0808 ET - The eurozone economy is already in a recession and consumer spending will be one of the drivers of the contraction, Oxford Economics' senior economist Tomas Dvorak says in a note. Eurozone consumer spending is expected to fall over the next two quarters as consumption fundamentals--real incomes and employment--weaken, while soaring energy prices keep inflation high, the economist says. Oxford Economics forecasts consumption will then gradually recover from the second quarter of 2023, but a weak carryover will result in a meager rise of 0.1% in 2023 and 2.3% over 2024. The main driver of consumption growth in the second half of 2023 will be the pick-up in real incomes as inflation slows and employment growth resumes, the economist says. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0737 ET - German Bund yields have some more leeway to rise as the priced inflation environment on a medium-term horizon looks a bit too benign, says Florian Spaete, senior bond strategist at \uc2 Generali Investments\uc2  . "Moreover, the sharply deteriorating supply environment is seen to trigger somewhat higher yields," he writes in a note. That said, \uc2 Generali Investments\uc2  sees some signs that the phase of sustained and steady rising yields is slowly coming to an end, he says. "Overall, we do not see an imminent end of the bear market but the leeway for much higher government bond yields appears limited," he says. The 10-year Bund yield is trading about 2 basis points higher at 2.139%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0732 ET - The dollar could rise as Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  is unlikely to provide explicit guidance about slowing the pace of interest rate rises at Wednesday's meeting, \uc2 MUFG Bank\uc2  says. "Core consumer price inflation currently stands at a cyclical high and it will therefore likely be deemed as premature to give even a hint that the battle on inflation is being won," \uc2 MUFG\uc2  analyst \uc2 Derek Halpenny\uc2  says in a note. With the labor market also showing limited signs of softening, the Fed might be compelled to disappoint those expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pivot on its aggressive tightening stance, which should support the dollar, he says. The Fed announces its rate decision at 1800 GMT. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 02, 2022 09:31 ET (13:31 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020221102eib2002d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
