\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar sags as Fed decision looms; yen and Aussie rise\b0\par\par\uc2 841 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2022\par 07:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 2 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar slipped from near a one-week peak versus major peers on Wednesday, with traders on tenterhooks before a looming \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  rate decision that should also give clues on the future policy path.\par \par \uc2 The yen outperformed, seeing a sudden burst of strength mid-morning \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  time, with traders on alert for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the Fed meeting.\par \par \uc2 The risk-sensitive Australian and New Zealand dollars also rose strongly, buoyed by a rally in Chinese equity markets.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index - which gauges the greenback against a basket of six counterparts that includes the yen, euro and sterling - eased 0.14% to 111.32, but was still not far below Tuesday's high of 111.78, the strongest level since Oct. 25.\par \par \uc2 The index rode a yo-yo overnight, dropping fast going into the European open only to recover after U.S. data pointed to continued price pressures, dampening speculation of a Fed pivot this year. U.S. job openings unexpectedly rose, suggesting wage growth stays elevated, while construction spending staged a surprise rebound.\par \par \uc2 Investors widely expect the Fed to raise its benchmark interest rate by 75 basis points (bps) on Wednesday, the fourth such increase in a row. But for the December meeting, the futures market is split on the odds of a 75- or 50-bps increase amid recent suggestions from Fed officials of a potential slowdown in the tightening pace.\par \par \uc2 "In the Fed's view, putting the U.S. into a recession is still a lesser evil than not tackling entrenched price pressures," Chris Weston, head of research at Pepperstone, wrote in a client note.\par \par \uc2 "It seems highly unlikely that the Fed will want to promote a positive reaction in risky assets, and the risks to markets in my mind are skewed to a hawkish reaction \u8211\'20\'13 equity up, bond yields and the USD lower."\par \par \uc2 The dollar index has surged more than 15% this year as the Fed has hiked rates hard, crushing other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and heaping pressure on the global economy.\par \par \uc2 YEN JUMPS\par \par \uc2 The yen has been particularly vulnerable to dollar strength, spurring the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September for the first time since 1998.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities are widely considered to have waded in several times again in October to pull the yen back from 32-year lows just shy of 152 per dollar, although they declined to confirm any action.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped suddenly by about half a yen to 147.4 per dollar, and then extended those gains as far as 147.165 before pulling back.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was last down 0.44% at 147.575 yen.\par \par \uc2 "This doesn't look like \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to me," said \uc2 Ray Attrill\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "On the three occasions that we know about, the \uc2 BOJ\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in enormous size and repeatedly, and if we were seeing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now - unless the pattern has changed - I would expect we would see much more significant movements that would be continuing now."\par \par \uc2 The initial leap in the yen coincided with several events that could have played a role, analysts said, including a drop in long-term \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields, to which the dollar-yen rate is strongly correlated.\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials were also speaking in parliament, including \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2 , who said that increasing flexibility in the yield curve control policy could be a future option, and Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2 , who said later in the day that the government was concerned about steady yen depreciation as well as speculative moves.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  also released minutes of its latest policy meeting around that time, with a member saying the bank must be vigilant for an inflation overshoot, possibly caused by yen weakness.\par \par \uc2 North Korea fired several missiles around the same time too.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the euro edged up 0.14% to $0.9887, but was still close to the prior session's one-week low at $0.98535.\par \par \uc2 Sterling rose 0.24% to $1.1513, but remained not far from Tuesday's one-week low of $1.14365.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of England\uc2  announces its policy decision on Thursday, and markets expect a 75-bps increase there as well, followed by a slowdown to a 50-bps pace in December.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie advanced 0.43% to $0.6421, with Hong Kong leading a rally in Chinese stocks on Wednesday as speculation started to build about an economic reopening.\par \par \uc2 China is a major customer of Australia's commodity exports, making Australian assets, particularly the Australian dollar, a proxy for market participants to gain exposure to China.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi dollar rose 0.46% to $0.5866, garnering additional support after an upbeat jobs report reinforced the case for a super-sized increase in interest rates this month from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Buckland; Editing by Gerry Doyle and Himani Sarkar) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-11-2T07:19:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221102eib2015ih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
