\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Japan spent a record 43.2 billion euros in latest yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Tokyo, Nov. 1. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record 6.35 trillion yen (about 43.2 billion euros) on various monetary \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October to maintain the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This represents the highest spending figure since September, when the Executive disbursed 2.84 trillion yen (19 billion euros), an amount believed to have been spent mainly on the monetary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last September 22, the first involving the purchase of yen since 1998.\par \par \uc2 The October figure is in line with estimates made by analysts regarding the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the middle of that month, which led the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to suddenly fall to the low 146 yen range against the dollar, fueling rumors of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was not officially confirmed by the government.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  confirmed that figure Tuesday at a press conference and said that "sometimes \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not announced immediately afterwards to maximize the effect of smoothing sudden fluctuations."\par \par \uc2 "Excessive fluctuations due to speculation cannot be tolerated. We will closely monitor trends in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and take appropriate action," Suzuki continued.\par \par \uc2 The sharp fluctuations in October and comments by the Japanese Finance Minister suggest that there were several \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although no details were provided.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 22 when the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breached the 145 units per dollar barrier. That was its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2011 aimed at supporting the value of the and the first involving purchases of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998.\par \par \uc2 Among the factors behind this accelerated depreciation of the yen is the growing distance between the monetary policies of the U.S. and the main European central banks - which are opting for aggressive rate hikes - and that of the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BoJ), which is opting to maintain its ultra-low rate strategy. EFE\par \par \uc2 emg-yk/mra/gcf\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221101eib1003cl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
