\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-INTERVIEW-Japan has tools to smooth out yen moves, says ex-finance ministry exec\b0\par\par\uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2022\par 00:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story from late Monday with no changes to text)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't keep yen at set level - Kinoshita\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 BOJ\uc2  likely to eventually exit ultra-loose policy - Kinoshita\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Path towards exit from easy policy must be steady, cautious\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kinoshita seen as among candidates to join new \uc2 BOJ\uc2  leadership\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Yoshifumi Takemoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 31 (Reuters) - Japanese authorities cannot control yen levels with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but they have various tools to smooth out volatile moves driven by speculators, former top finance ministry bureaucrat Yasushi Kinoshita said on Monday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been conducting yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since September to prevent a sharp slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  driven by the gap between steadily tighter U.S. monetary policy and the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's continued ultra-loose policy.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot and isn't intended to move the yen significantly up and down, or keep it at a certain level for a sustained period of time," said Kinoshita, seen as a candidate to join the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's leadership next year.\par \par \uc2 "Rather, it's aimed at preventing speculators from triggering volatile moves," said Kinoshita, who played a key role when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011.\par \par \uc2 "Japanese authorities are armed with the wisdom and various tools to fight speculators," he told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Kinoshita said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must eventually exit its ultra-loose policy but added that the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  must tread carefully and coordinate closely with the government in withdrawing stimulus.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone understands the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  must eventually head for the exit," Kinoshita said.\par \par \uc2 "It must proceed steadily but cautiously," he said, as withdrawing fiscal and monetary support simultaneously and too hastily would hurt the fragile economy.\par \par \uc2 Kinoshita, who retains close ties with incumbent policymakers, served as vice finance minister for about a year from 2013, when \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  deployed his "bazooka" stimulus programme to eradicate deflation.\par \par \uc2 He is seen as one candidate to join the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's leadership when Kuroda's term ends next April and those of his two deputies run out in March.\par \par \uc2 Some investors bet the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will start to phase out its massive stimulus upon dovish governor Kuroda's departure, as prolonged ultra-low rates drive unwelcome yen falls that boost import costs.\par \par \uc2 "Given that what the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is doing now is unprecedented, it won't be easy," Kinoshita said of the likelihood of a smooth lift-off from ultra-low rates.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  sets a negative short-term rate target and caps the 10-year bond yield around zero, remaining an outlier among a wave of central banks raising rates to combat soaring inflation.\par \par \uc2 Kinoshita was director-general of the international bureau when the finance ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011 to stem a sharp yen rise that was hurting exports. He is currently chairman of the government-backed \uc2 Development Bank of Japan\uc2 . (Reporting by Leika Kihara; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-11-3T23:32:50.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221031eiav04ybh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
