\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Asian Shares Mixed As China Worries Persist\b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Asian shares ended mixed on Thursday as Fed pivot hopes were offset by concerns over China's growth trajectory.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was pinned near one-month lows on bets of less hawkish Fed while oil slipped in Asian trade after having surged nearly 3 percent on Wednesday, bolstered by record crude exports in the United States.\par \par \uc2 China's Shanghai Composite index slipped 0.55 percent to 2,982.90 after data showed profits at China's industrial firms sank for a third consecutive month in September.Power generating giant \uc2 Datang International Power Generation\uc2  plunged 10 percent after reporting weak third-quarter earnings.\par \par \uc2 The yuan briefly touched a 1-1/2-week high against the dollar before reversing course amid reports that Chinese cities from Wuhan in central China to Xining in the northwest are tightening curbs against growing COVID outbreaks.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's Hang Seng index climbed 0.72 percent to 15,427.94.\par \par \uc2 Japanese shares fell amid reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the government and the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Focus shifted to an interest rate decision by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  on Friday, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to stick with rock-bottom rates.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei average eased 0.32 percent to settle at 27,345.24 while the broader Topix index closed 0.66 percent lower at 1,905.56. Automakers led losses, with \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2 , \uc2 Nissan\uc2  and \uc2 Honda\uc2  falling 1-2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Seoul stocks rallied after data showed the country's economy grew 0.3 percent in the September quarter backed mostly by consumer spending and investment in facilities.\par \par \uc2 The Kospi average jumped 1.74 percent to 2,288.78, extending gains for a second straight session.\par \par \uc2 Samsung SDI\uc2  topped the gainers list to close 7.4 percent higher at 727,000 won while chip giant \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  lost 4.2 percent after reporting sluggish third-quarter earnings earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Australian shares rose to their highest levels in over a month. The resources-heavy S&P/ASX 200 rose half a percent to 6,845.10 as gains in commodity prices on the back of a weaker dollar helped lift miners and energy stocks. The broader All Ordinaries index gained 0.53 percent to close at 7,042.30.\par \par \uc2 Lynas Rare Earths\uc2  shares soared 5.6 percent after the rare-earths miner reported a 35 percent jump in first-quarter revenue on strong rare earths demand.\par \par \uc2 Across the Tasman, New Zealand's benchmark S&P NZX-50 index inched up 0.49 percent to 11,100.52.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks ended mostly lower overnight, as warnings from the tech behemoths overshadowed investor optimism over falling Treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 The tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite showed wild swings before closing 2 percent lower following negative earnings news from tech giants \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 shed 0.7 percent while the Dow finished marginally higher to stretch its winning streak to a fourth session on the back of better-than-expected quarterly earnings from \uc2 Visa\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221027eiar0073i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
