ht\uc2  not contradictory \u8226\'20\'22 Suzuki: \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in constant touch with U.S. on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \u8226\'20\'22 Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has done USD/JPY bulls a great favour GBP/USD near 1.13 before Sunak takes over as Britain's PM \u8226\'20\'22 Cable holds near 1.1300 before Sunak replaces Truss as UK PM this am (BST) \u8226\'20\'22 See: 1.1273-1.1341marks intra-day range-to-date \u8226\'20\'22 1.1259-1.1402 was Monday's range (high before low). 1.1060 was Friday's low \u8226\'20\'22 IMM speculators raised net GBP short to four-week high before Truss resigned \u8226\'20\'22 See: Fed/\uc2 BoE\uc2  rate decisions next week: 75 bps hikes expected \u8226\'20\'22 Fall in gilt yields shows credibility coming back-\uc2 BoE\uc2 's Ramsden AUD/USD holds above 0.63 after low-drama Aussie budget \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD remains above 0.6300 following low-drama Australian budget \u8226\'20\'22 See: 0.6341 was Asian session high \u8226\'20\'22 There are large 0.6300 option expiries Wednesday/Thursday (A$1 bln total) \u8226\'20\'22 0.6273 was Monday's low, as China stock losses hurt risk-sensitive AUD \u8226\'20\'22 SSEC closed flat today. 0.6410 was Monday's high (pre-China stock losses) \u8226\'20\'22 0.6212 was last Friday's low (before suspected BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in USD/JPY) \uc2 BoE\uc2  might set off sterling fireworks next week \uc2 The Bank of England\uc2  might send the pound fizzing or fizzling with its interest rate decision and quarterly Monetary Policy Report next week. Money markets currently fully price a 75 basis point rate hike to 3.0% to follow last month's 50 bps rise -- delivered a day before the UK "mini-budget" upended sterling and gilts. A 100 bps increase on Nov. 3 might lift the pound -- albeit perhaps only temporarily, while another 50 bps hike could weigh on it. The \uc2 BoE\uc2 's rate verdict will come three days after the government's scheduled Halloween budget to plug a black hole in the UK public finances, and two days after the \uc2 BoE\uc2 's Quantitative Tightening programme starts. CFTC data at the end of last week showed IMM speculators raised their net GBP short position to its highest level since the UK "mini-budget" in the week ended Oct. 18, two days before \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  resigned as Britain's Prime Minister. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3N6o2GH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  The foundations for a bigger dollar rise are in place The dollar was supported when U.S. investors pared assets as interest rates rose and may now strengthen further as investors pile back into those same assets and thus encourage the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to pursue its aim of bringing inflation back to target. The Dow Jones index (DJI) dropped from January's record peak at 36,952 to 28,660 earlier this month, supporting a 21% gain in the dollar index with the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  lifting interest rates from 0.25% to 3.25%. In the last two weeks, though, DJI has surged almost 3,000 points - a move more in keeping with a boom than the slowdown that traders think will influence the Federal Reserve to pause. This effective boom is grounds for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push hard in its aim to bring inflation back to a currently far distant inflation target. Markets influenced by interest rates are moving in that direction, with derivatives pricing 5% interest rates for the first time last week and the yield on benchmark U.S. debt reaching a new 2022 peak at 4.33%. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders have been influenced by \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has forced them to reduce bets the dollar will go up, and likely encouraged them to add to bets it will drop ahead of this week's \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting. That leaves them less prepared for the likelihood the dollar continues to rise and may spur an acceleration in the pace of the rally. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3U9XoiL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-28T10:52:46.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221025eiap027bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
