\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-BoJ stealth  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  maybe new norm\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2022\par 05:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oct 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently switched tack in how it conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Rather than confirm action as in the past, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  have left the market guessing as to whether or not it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a particular occasion..\par \par \uc2 Granted, reports of the size of transactions on Friday and Monday, and moves in USD/JPY, leave no doubt in the minds of most that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually took place. That said, this new strategy leaves open the possibility of smaller, perhaps more frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and could keep market participants cautious for longer.\par \par \uc2 Banks, which operate on behalf of Japanese authorities during \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are likely to remain mum on whether they were used for fear of being blacklisted by the BoJ. Monday saw especially good USD sales by one major Japanese mega-bank. Friday may have seen all three of Japan's major banks in action given the reported scope of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ..\par \par \uc2 Such a strategy by Japanese authorities is not surprising given the market propensity to view \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as opportunities to buy USD anew. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday took USD/JPY down from 151.95 to 146.23 and was followed by a bounce later to 148.46. Monday's Asia action, which took USD/JPY from 149.70 to 145.56, then saw a bounce later to 149.45 in London. Related,.\par \par \uc2 No doubt a number of speculators were forced out of USD longs post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Japanese authorities are likely to continue with this strategy in an effort to punish speculators and slow JPY depreciation in light of diverging \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies..\par \par \uc2 * For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Haruya Ida is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-28T03:05:40.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221025eiap00i21\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
