\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Sterling at 6-week high as Sunak becomes PM, while dollar sags\b0\par\par\uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2022\par 21:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By John McCrank\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Sterling rallied to a six-week high on Tuesday on improved risk sentiment as \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  became Britain's prime minister, while the dollar fell to a three-week low as weakening U.S. economic data cooled expectations on the pace of future U.S. rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 The potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility is elevated this week, with central banks in the euro zone and Canada expected to hike rates by 75 basis points, and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  set to maintain ultra-low interest rates to support its fragile economy.\par \par \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  became Britain's third prime minister in two months on Tuesday, tasked with tackling a mounting economic crisis and a warring political party.\par \par \uc2 Sterling surged to its strongest level since Sept. 15, and was last up 1.66% at $1.147, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists expect the pound's climb to be short-lived.\par \par \uc2 "Beyond a brief honeymoon phase rally, I think the daunting road ahead for the UK economy is likely to cap sterling gains," said Joe Manimbo, senior market analyst at Convera.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was broadly weaker amid signs that Federal Reserve rate hikes are slowing the world's biggest economy. The greenback slid into negative territory after data showed that U.S. home prices sank in August as surging mortgage rates sapped demand.\par \par \uc2 "U.S. economic data is deteriorating and that is helping push down Treasury yields," said \uc2 Edward Moya\uc2 , senior market analyst at Oanda. "If the data keeps on getting uglier, the December FOMC meeting debate might not be between a half point increase and 75 basis point hike, but with a quarter point rise and 50 basis-point boost."\par \par \uc2 The Fed is expected to raise rates by 75 basis points for a fourth-straight time at its Nov. 1-2 meeting.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the greenback against six major peers, was down 0.822% at 110.94 at 3:10 p.m. EDT (1910 GMT).\par \par \uc2 The euro strengthened to a 20-day high ahead of Thursday's \uc2 ECB\uc2  meeting, where a three-quarter point hike is expected by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it seeks to rein in red-hot inflation.\par \par \uc2 The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was last up 0.87% at 0.99595.\par \par \uc2 "Warm weather is fueling (relative) optimism about the energy crisis, even if Germany\u8217\'20\'19s IFO data is deep into recessionary territory," said Kit Juckes, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Societe General\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Ifo Institute for Economic Research said Germany is heading into recession, forecasting that Europe's biggest economy will contract by 0.6% in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 YEN AND YUAN\par \par \uc2 The yen firmed against the dollar after suspected \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday and Monday.\par \par \uc2 A retreat this week in long-term Treasury yields also helped support the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the policy background for yen weakness is likely to be put into stark relief in coming days, with the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  expected to stick to monetary stimulus on Friday.\par \par \uc2 At 147.96 yen, the dollar was down from a 32-year high against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 151.94 on Friday, which appeared to trigger successive bouts of \uc2 BOJ\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on whether it had ordered \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days, though it did confirm action in September, which was the first yen-buying foray by Japanese authorities since 1998.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, extended the weakness seen since Chinese leader \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 's choice of leadership team at the twice-a-decade Communist Party Congress raised fears that growth will be sacrificed for ideology-driven policies.\par \par \uc2 The onshore yuan slid to its lowest in nearly 15 years on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the lowest mid-point since 2008. The offshore yuan dipped to a record low of 7.375 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by John McCrank in New York and Joice Alves in London; Editing by David Goodman, Bernadette Baum and Nick Zieminski) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-25T20:42:52.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221025eiap04fyd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
