\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  sees \uc2 BOJ\uc2  easing and govt  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  not contradictory\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2022\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Policy mix between government and \uc2 BOJ\uc2  seen in doubt\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Yen hovers near 32-yr lows vs dlr despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Suzuki says in constant touch with U.S. on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Estimates show record spending on yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimates, paragraphs 9-10)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said on Tuesday there was no policy contradiction between his ministry's yen-buying to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) printing money to sustain its ultra-loose monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 "Monetary easing aimed at sustainable and stable price hikes including wage growth, and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to excessive market moves, are different in terms of policy objectives, and thus they are not contradictory," Suzuki said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy was aimed at achieving price stability, not targeting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 Suzuki made the remarks at a news conference when asked whether the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's monetary easing may cause excessive yen weakening and whether the policy mix between the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was having the intended effects.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is set to maintain ultra-low interest rates at its two-day policy meeting ending on Friday to support the fragile economy, even at the cost of accelerating an unwelcome fall in the yen to new 32-year lows.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers have voiced concerns about the impact of a weak yen on living costs. And investors regard the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  as an outlier for pursuing ultra-low rates while central banks elsewhere have raised rates to combat soaring inflation.\par \par \uc2 Global commodity costs stemming from Russia's invasion of Ukraine and the weak yen account equally for rising prices, Suzuki said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been conducting yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the yen against sharp declines, which have been driven by the widening divergence between Japanese and U.S. interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Japan likely spent up to 900 billion yen ($6 billion) on its second straight day of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, bringing total yen-buying since last month to as much as 9.2 trillion yen, market estimates show.\par \par \uc2 Authorities' so-called stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in rapid succession has underscored their resolve to fight what they have characterised as "intolerable and speculative" yen-selling, although the impact has proved short-lived.\par \par \uc2 IN TOUCH WITH U.S.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities are in constant touch with U.S. counterparts and stand ready to take appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market against volatile yen moves, Suzuki said.\par \par \uc2 The minister repeated that the government would not tolerate excessively volatile yen moves driven by speculative trading.\par \par \uc2 Japan and the United States have reaffirmed a \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  (G7) agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Suzuki said, adding that he and Yellen both believed \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be set by markets.\par \par \uc2 "If we leave unattended sharply volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, driven by speculative trading, that would affect companies and households," Suzuki said.\par \par \uc2 He also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at smoothing market volatility, signalling that Tokyo was not targeting a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in deciding when to step into the market to buy yen. ($1 = 148.8700 yen) (Additional reporting by Daiki Iga; Writing by Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Jacqueline Wong, Sam Holmes & Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-25T11:15:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221025eiap0076d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
