\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened \highlight\uc2 , buying yen in  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market Friday -sources\b0\par\par\uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2022\par 02:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Corrects Saturday story to show dollar, not yen, fall in paragraph 3)\par \par \uc2 By Shinji Kitamura and Yoshifumi Takemoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to buy yen for the second time in a month after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 32-year low near 152 to the dollar, a government official and another person familiar with the matter told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Japan has been attempting to shore up the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sticks with ultra-low interest rates, countering a global trend of tightening monetary policy and widening the gap between U.S. and Japanese interest rates.\par \par \uc2 After the dollar rose to 151.94 yen, its highest since 1990, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove the greenback down more than 7 yen to a low of 144.50 yen. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was last down 1.8% at 147.34 yen.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in several stages from around 9:35 p.m. (1235 GMT), one source said.\par \par \uc2 "We are maintaining our stance of being ready to take appropriate action against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility," Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2  told reporters on Saturday after meeting with Australia's Anthony Albanese, reiterating that such volatility could not be tolerated.\par \par \uc2 Kishida declined to comment further, saying, "I will not make any detailed comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 " when asked about Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, Masato Kanda, also declined to say whether the MOF had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We won't comment now on whether or not we conducted an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kanda, the vice finance minister for international affairs, told Reuters on Saturday, saying that this was a stance the MOF has stuck to over the past several weeks.\par \par \uc2 He added that the ministry would not confirm whether an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken place for some time yet, signalling possible "stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to engage in a war of nerves against investors selling the yen.\par \par \uc2 The MOF also bought yen on Sept. 22, as investors focussed on the widening divergence between the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's ultra-loose monetary policy and the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's aggressive rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  and Kanda have repeatedly signalled the government's readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , warning against excessive volatility. Suzuki said before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday the authorities were ready to act "strictly" against speculators.\par \par \uc2 Many market players doubt whether Tokyo can reverse the yen's downtrend with solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $1.33 trillion in foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  industrial powers agreed this month to closely monitor recent volatility but stopped short of indicating they were prepared for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record 3.6 trillion yen ($24 billion) in the September action, Tokyo money market brokerage firms estimated.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 147.6400 yen) (Reporting by Shinji Kitamura, Yoshifumi Takemoto, Tetsushi Kajimoto, Kiyoshi Takenaka and Kentaro Sugiyama; Writing by Sakura Murakami and Leika Kihara; Editing by William Mallard)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-27T00:35:15.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221024eiao002xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
