\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-COLUMN-Japan faces battle royale with funds on yen: McGeever\b0\par\par\uc2 747 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2022\par 13:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats column with no changes to text)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 ORLANDO, Fla., Oct 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's historic \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sept. 22 failed to stem the wave of speculative bets against the yen, culminating in a fresh 32-year low through 150.00 per dollar and a second round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 Against the backdrop of a yawning U.S.-Japanese interest rate and bond yield chasm, however, hedge funds and speculators are unlikely to be deterred by the Bank of Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  from betting on further yen weakness.\par \par \uc2 Right on cue, a suspected third bout of \uc2 BOJ\uc2 /MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early Asian trading on Monday after the yen had slumped back towards the 150.00 level underscores the fight Japan has on its hands to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The evolution of \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  positioning since last month's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a deeper dive into the latest CFTC figures for the week to Oct. 18 - three days before \uc2 BOJ\uc2 /MOF's second salvo - back this up.\par \par \uc2 The most recent CFTC report shows that funds increased their net short yen position to almost 95,000 contracts, the largest bet against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early June. It is a wager worth almost $8 billion.\par \par \uc2 A short position is essentially a wager that an asset's price will fall, and a long position is a bet it will rise.\par \par \uc2 The increase of more than 17,000 contracts from the prior week in net shorts was the most bearish shift in five weeks. Significantly, it was driven almost entirely by fresh short positions rather than longs being cut.\par \par \uc2 Funds increased their gross short positions by more than 17,000 contracts. There have only been four bigger moves this year. In aggregate, funds' short position of almost 125,000 contracts is the largest since November last year.\par \par \uc2 "The effects of yen buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have already diminished," NatWest's Yoshio Takahashi wrote on Friday. "Yen buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is intended to control the speed of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements and not to actively bolster the yen, so investors are less on guard against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 FED-BOJ POLICY CHASM\par \par \uc2 The latest bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may flush out some short positions, which would be welcomed by Japanese officials keen to suppress speculation and "excessive" volatility.\par \par \uc2 But a look at CFTC positioning shifts around the Sept. 22 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first official yen purchases in 24 years - and subsequent moves in the yen's exchange rate are revealing.\par \par \uc2 In the following week, CFTC specs cut their short yen positions by almost 11,000 contracts. That was the biggest reduction in seven weeks, and one of the five largest this year.\par \par \uc2 But it failed to materially reduce the net speculative wager because funds also substantially reduced their long yen position.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, funds trimmed their net short yen position by only a few thousand contracts following the Sept. 22 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The latest CFTC data shows they evidently felt confident enough to load up on short yen positions again.\par \par \uc2 That \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cost \uc2 BOJ\uc2 /MOF almost $20 billion. So far, authorities have officially declined to confirm Friday's and Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , never mind the quantities involved. But many billions more are likely to have been spent.\par \par \uc2 Japan has $1.25 trillion of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, but Tokyo will be reluctant to dip too deeply into that stash. A doom loop could ensue whereby Japan sells Treasuries, U.S. yields rise, the dollar becomes more attractive, it appreciates, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in even greater size to support the yen.\par \par \uc2 Speculators know this. They also know that the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is the only G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to be raising interest rates, while the Fed is on track to raise rates to around 5%, according to current market expectations.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  estimate that the level of dollar/yen consistent with a 5% Fed terminal rate is around 150.00. They are dialing back their bullish stance on dollar/yen, but "also suggest buying the dip if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again causes USD/JPY to drop well below levels consistent with the envisaged Fed terminal rate."\par \par \uc2 (The opinions expressed here are those of the author, a columnist for Reuters.)\par \par \uc2 Related columns:\par \par \uc2 - Beware yen, global market ructions if Japan tweaks 'YCC' (Oct. 20)\par \par \uc2 - King dollar delivers bumper Q3 for macro hedge funds (Oct. 9)\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jacqueline Wong) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-24T12:30:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 