\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened \highlight\uc2  by buying yen in  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market on Friday: sources\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Shinji Kitamura and Yoshifumi Takemoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to buy yen for the second time in a month after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 32-year low near 152 units to the dollar, a government official and another person with knowledge of the matter told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Japan has been trying to prop up the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps interest rates ultra-low, bucking a global trend of tightening monetary policy and widening the gap with U.S. rates.\par \par \uc2 After the dollar rose to 151.94 yen, its highest level since 1990, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down more than seven yen to a low of 144.50 units. The greenback eventually gave up 1.8% to 147.34 yen.\par \par \uc2 The Finance Ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in several stages from around 21:35 local time (1235 GMT), a source said.\par \par \uc2 "We maintain our stance of being prepared to take appropriate measures against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility," Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2  told the media on Saturday after meeting with his Australian counterpart, Anthony Albanese, reiterating that such volatility could not be tolerated.\par \par \uc2 Kishida added that "I will not make any detailed comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " when asked about Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, Masato Kanda, also declined to say whether the Finance Ministry had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We are not going to comment now on whether or not we have made an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kanda, deputy finance minister for international affairs, told Reuters on Saturday, saying it was a stance held by the ministry in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 He added that the ministry would not confirm whether there was an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for some time, indicating a possible "stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to engage in a war of nerves against investors selling the yen.\par \par \uc2 The Finance Ministry also bought yen on Sept. 22 as investors focused on the growing divergence between the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's ultra-loose monetary policy and the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's aggressive rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  and Kanda have repeatedly signaled the government's readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , warning of excessive volatility. Suzuki said before Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the authorities were ready to act "strictly" against speculators.\par \par \uc2 Many market players doubt Tokyo can reverse the yen's downward trend with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone, even despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $1.33 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  industrial powers agreed this month to keep a close eye on recent volatility, but stopped short of indicating they were prepared for a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record 3.6 trillion yen ($24 billion) in September's action, according to estimates by Tokyo exchange market brokerage firms. (Reporting by Shinji Kitamura, Yoshifumi Takemoto, Tetsushi Kajimoto, Kiyoshi Takenaka and Kentaro Sugiyama; writing by Sakura Murakami and Leika Kihara; edited in English by Carlos Serrano)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221022eiam007ap\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
