\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2022\par 01:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Stocks Rise as Treasury Yields Dip \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors weighed the possibility of a slower pace of interest-rate increases and uneven corporate results. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed Set to Raise Rates by 0.75 Point and Debate Size of Future Hikes \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some officials have begun signaling their desire to slow down the pace of increases soon and to stop raising rates early next year to see how their moves this year are slowing the economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Yen rallies against the dollar as Japanese authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after hitting 32-year low \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese yen suddenly rallied against the U.S. dollar on Friday amid reports and widespread speculation that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yen after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tumbled to a fresh 32-year low against the greenback. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The U.S. Dollar is Wreaking Havoc \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE U.S. Dollar Index, which measures the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength against a basket of six other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is up 20.6% in the past 12 months, with the greenback thrashing major counterparts like the yen and pound in the process, while wreaking havoc all over the world. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Ukraine Strikes Occupied Kherson as More Civilians Flee \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ukrainian artillery struck the ferry crossing in the southern city of Kherson, the only regional capital captured by Moscow since the February invasion, as Russian forces pounded the cities of Zaporizhzhia and Kharkiv. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Investors Jump Into Turbocharged ETFs \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite a market rout, risky leveraged and inverse exchange-traded funds have raked in nearly $25 billion this year as investors seek to turbocharge their bets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Chinese Stock Traders Told Not to Disrupt Market Around Party Meeting \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brokers, fund managers received unofficial guidance about trading activity, to reduce market volatility \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Europe's Energy Shock Spurs Rethink of Liberalized Gas Markets \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rocked by its biggest energy shock since the 1970s, Europe is unpicking parts of a two-decade endeavor to foster a competitive market in natural gas. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Southern California's Notorious Container Ship Backup Ends \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The backup of container ships off Southern California's coast that was at the heart of U.S. supply chain congestion during the Covid-19 pandemic has effectively disappeared. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU Leaders Push Forward Plans to Tackle Gas Prices \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The summit discussed an emergency gas-price cap, with debate over how to support consumers without upending markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 21, 2022 19:00 ET (23:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020221021eial004eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
