22 CA Aug Retail Sales MM 0.7%, 0.2% f\u8217\'20\'19cast, -2.5% prev, -2.2% r\u8217\'20\'19vsd \u8226\'20\'22 CA Aug Retail Sales Ex-Autos MM 0.7%, 0.4% f\u8217\'20\'19cast, -3.1% prev, -2.5% r\u8217\'20\'19vsd Looking Ahead - Economic Data (GMT) \u8226\'20\'22 23 Oct 22:00 AU Oct Mfg \uc2 PMI\uc2  Flash 53.5 prev \u8226\'20\'22 23 Oct 22:00 AU Oct Services PMI Flash 50.6 prev \u8226\'20\'22 23 Oct 22:00 AU Oct Comp PMI Flash 50.9 prev Looking Ahead - Events, Other Releases (GMT) \u8226\'20\'22 22 Oct 09:00 \uc2 ECB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Lagarde participates in 'Mein Lieblingsst\u252\'00\'FCck' event at the Alte Oper Frankfurt \u8226\'20\'22 22 Oct 18:00 \uc2 BoE\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Catherine L Mann in conversation at the Marshall Society Speaker event in Cambridge, London \u8226\'20\'22 24 Oct 10:30 Germany's Robert Habeck and his Ukrainian counterpart, Yulia Svyrydenko, take part in a dialogue as part of the 5th German-Ukrainian Business Forum in Berlin Macro Themes In Play \u8226\'20\'22 The dollar fell on Friday behind a stunning plunge in USD/JPY from a 32-year high of 151.94 down to 144.50, amid what appeared to be waves of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling mixed with longs being stopped out and a sharp pullback in Fed rate-hike pricing. \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment but the Nikkei newspaper said the government and the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted yen-buying, dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and officials had previously said that they can take action without making an announcement. \u8226\'20\'22 And unlike prior USD/JPY pullbacks since the Sept. 22 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that officials announced, those buying dips were run through the mill in the spike below the daily tenkan and kijun lines that had previously been supportive. \u8226\'20\'22 However, residual demand remains due to very attractive Treasury-JGB yield spreads and starkly bullish divergence between Fed and JGB policies. \u8226\'20\'22 Adding to the broader dollar drop, a Wall Street Journal article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://on.wsj.com/3EW4jrk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  raised speculation that the Fed's string of 75bp rate hikes could end with November's meeting, with officials considering how to signal that smaller rate hikes would follow. \u8226\'20\'22 Shorter-term Treasury yields and 2023 Fed hike pricing fell. The market had projected peak rates above 5% but that fell below 4.9% subsequently, with a 50bp December move favored over a 75bp. \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 San Francisco Fed\uc2  President \uc2 Mary Daly\uc2  later said getting the Fed funds rate up to the 4.5% - 5.0% range next year is reasonable, but noted numerous factors that could influence policy before then. \u8226\'20\'22 Two-year Treasury yields fell 11bp, earlier hitting a 15-year high at 4.637%. The drop in yields lifted most riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though sterling lagged gains in high betas like the Australian dollar, which was up 1.1%. \u8226\'20\'22 Sterling was up about 0.2% versus EUR/USD's 0.5% rise and the roughly 1.2% fall in USD/JPY. Two-year and 10-year Gilts yields surged 28bp and 23bp as economic and political risk premia rebounded, overriding any drag from tumbling UK retail sales, that might have been skewed by the Queen's funeral. \u8226\'20\'22 U.S. data thins out into month-end, though \uc2 ECB\uc2  and \uc2 BOJ\uc2  meetings are on Thursday and Friday. Commentary and Analysis EUR/USD-BOJ, Fed, rates help longs gain traction \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD fell in Europe's morning, NY opened near 0.9750, slide extended \u8226\'20\'22 Pair hit a 6-session low of 0.9705 on EBS due to US rates, US$ gains \u8226\'20\'22 Sharp rally ensued on \uc2 BOJ\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY fell to 144.50 on EBS, helps EUR/USD turned positive, hit 0.9868 \u8226\'20\'22 WSJ article helped soften US rates, US$ \u8226\'20\'22 Comments from Fed' Daly also weighed down US rates and US$ \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD pulled back from the high, sat near 0.9835 late, was up +0.47% \u8226\'20\'22 Daily bull hammer formed, daily RSI diverged; are concerns for shorts \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD longs hope seeds of Fed doubts actually bloom USD/JPY-Tumbled 5% from 32-yr high on Fed rethink, suspected MoF sales \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY up to 32-yr high at 151.94 before a plunge to 144.50 on EBS \u8226\'20\'22 Huge intraday swings on the way down amid suspected MoF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8226\'20\'22 Japanese officials not confirming it, but Nikkei source said it was \u8226\'20\'22 Drop aggravated by WSJ story about Fed getting ready to slow rate hikes \u8226\'20\'22 Unlike other USD/JPY dips since Sept. 22 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , supports gave way \u8226\'20\'22 Buyers into tenkan and kijun at 148.22/6.12 run over by 144.50 final low \u8226\'20\'22 Big rebound since above 148 in a harrowing pre-weekend trading day \u8226\'20\'22 Surge in volatility came as London was closing, adding to the mayhem \u8226\'20\'22 Fri's low was lowest since Oct. 5, erased almost all of Oct's gains \u8226\'20\'22 Also more than 61.8% of 140.31-151.94 rise from Sept. 22's spike low \u8226\'20\'22 Two-year Tsy-JGB yield spreads by 4.5% still attracts carry trades Sterling looks past political woes, rallies on lower US yield outlook \u8226\'20\'22 GBP$ ending NorAm +0.22% at 1.1264, Friday range 1.1300-1.1060 \u8226\'20\'22 Early NY slide to minor Fib supt at 1.1061 reversed amid falling UST yields \u8226\'20\'22 Sterling pares politics-driven slide as US yields dip \u8226\'20\'22 Broad USD selling on lower Fed rate outlook trump UK political angst \u8226\'20\'22 Despite GBP$ rally puts in 5th straight lwr high, lwr low which is bearish \u8226\'20\'22 Resistance at 1.13 Friday high, 1.1356 Oct 19 high, 55-DMA 1.1494 caps \u8226\'20\'22 Support at 10-HMA by 1.1179, Friday low 1.1060, 1.0910 50% of 1.0327-1.1493 AUD/USD-BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Fed influence drive a change of direction \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD fell overnight on rising US rates, US$ gains \u8226\'20\'22 NY opened near 0.6255, slide extended, 4-session low of 0.6212 was hit \u8226\'20\'22 US$ sales emerged on \uc2 BOJ\uc2  USD/JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8226\'20\'22 WSJ Fed piece weighs down US rates, U$ \u8226\'20\'22 Fed Pres. Daly comments help maintain bear pressure on US$ \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD turned positive, rallied above the 10-DMA and Oct. 20 daily high \u8226\'20\'22 0.6379 traded, 21-DMA left untouched before pair neared 0.6360 late \u8226\'20\'22 Techs lean bullish; daily, monthly bull hammers form, daily RSI diverged Dollar tumbles vs yen in suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  USD/JPY tumbled from its 32-year high of 151.94 on Friday in a drop seen as suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also followed a sharp retreat in Fed rate hike bets. USD/JPY had already run into resistance from the upper 10-week Bolli at 152.06 before Fed rate hike expectations retreated in the wake of a WSJ article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://on.wsj.com/3EW4jrk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , which softened the dollar. Tick charts since then show huge downward spikes with hallmarks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though the MoF has said it can take action without announcing it. USD/JPY's next support is the daily kijun, now at 146.12. This year's 32% rise suggests scope for a correction. But eventually highly attractive Treasury-JGB yields spreads should limit losses. The WSJ article pointed out that the Fed will have to back off aggressive 75bp rate hikes soon. The Fed rate ceiling fell back from above 5% earlier on Friday, but remains above the Fed's median 2023 dot plot at 4.75%. The BoJ's -0.1% policy rate and QE to cap JGB yields mean Treasury-JGB yield spreads should remain very attractive. Chart: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3MVjbYP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  EUR/USD longs hope seeds of Fed doubts actually bloom EUR/USD fell to a 6-session low of 0.9705 on Friday but then rallied sharply to turn positive on the session as investors once again tried to anticipate a potential shift from Fed. A large wave of dollar selling, led by USD/JPY, followed the release of a Wall Street Journal piece suggesting the Fed would deliver a 75bp rate increase in November while also debating whether and how to downsize future hikes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://on.wsj.com/3EW4jrk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 U.S. interest rates turned lower after an earlier rally and March 2023 Eurodollar prices turned positive as traders priced in a lower terminal Fed rate, while \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  2-year yields fell from a 15-year high of 4.639% and traded below 4.20%. The dollar erased gains versus most major and many emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . EUR/USD rallied back above the 10- and 21-day moving averages. EUR/USD technical signals highlight upside risks. Daily RSI diverged on Friday's low and a daily bull hammer candle formed. A monthly doji candle has formed, which could be a sign the down trend will reverse. Should the Fed indeed alter its current hawkish policy EUR/USD is likely to see big gains. Chart: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3CSjH5l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  Chart of the Day (GBP/USD) Sterling fell on Friday as political uncertainty ahead of yet another Tory leadership race weighed, putting in play the Oct. 13 low at 1.1061 and potentially a test of Fib support by 1.0910, though a dip in U.S. yields may stalled such a move momentarily. GBP/USD bounced more than a big figure off early NorAm session lows, rising to 1.1195 as the dollar pared gains amid a drop in \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields, though Eurodollar futures indicate another 75bp Fed rate hike on Nov 2. The GBP/USD rally off session lows by 1.1060 is likely weekend position lightening and its rise into the European close lagged other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovering against the dollar. UK faces considerable political, inflation and growth uncertainties, and expectations of the \uc2 BoE\uc2  hiking more than 300bp by H2 2023 foreshadow economic hardship and more sterling declines even if the political vista clears. A close below the Oct. 13 low at 1.1060 would put the 50% Fib of 1.0327-1.1493 at 1.0910 in focus. Below there, bears would gain momentum for a drop toward the lower 30-day Bolli at 1.0760 and the Sept. 28 low at 1.0539. Chart: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3MSHWVr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-24T19:13:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221021eial03v9x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
