\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-USD/JPY above 150, no action yet but caution prevails\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2022\par 04:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oct 21 (Reuters) - USD/JPY broke above 150.00 Thursday, reaching a fresh 32-year high of 150.29 on EBS in New York. The move elicited no actual \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities, only ramped up jaw-boning in an effort to slow further gains.\par \par \uc2 The lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not really surprising given broad U.S. dollar strength and another leg up in Treasury yields. With the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  remaining hawkish, U.S. yields looking set to climb further and Japanese monetary policy staying very easy, both Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are well aware of the futility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt JPY weakness.\par \par \uc2 This does not imply \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Any USD/JPY spikes could trigger strong action with the official stance now focusing on excessive volatility and speculative moves. To wit, USD/JPY is up about 32% this year from its 113.47 January low.\par \par \uc2 Anecdotal evidence suggests importer demand remains strong, especially on USD/JPY dips. Some Japanese investors too look to be collecting dollars on dips, along with speculative players.\par \par \uc2 The bias for USD/JPY remains higher, and dealers see tests to the upside continuing. Resistance is likely from 150.50 with more at 151.00. August 1990 saw a high of 151.58, July 1990 152.23, June 1990 155.77, May 1990 159.60 and April 1990 a high of 160.35. All these levels will be targets for spec players along with any option barriers on the way.\par \par \uc2 For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Haruya Ida is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own. Editing by Sonali Desai and Ewen Chew)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-24T02:38:59.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221021eial00bhx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
