\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar falls against yen amid rumors of \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Saqib Iqbal Ahmed\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 21 (Reuters) - The dollar was falling against the yen on Friday, posting its biggest daily decline against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in nearly three years, which traders and strategists believed was because Japanese authorities may be in the market to stem the slide in their battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The yen rose as high as 144.8 units to the dollar in late morning U.S. trading, but then posted a smaller gain of 2.2% to 147.055 yen.\par \par \uc2 * "I think this is an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \uc2 Karl Schamotta\uc2 , chief market strategist at Corpay in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 * "We're seeing a lot of dollar selling and the yen is moving almost vertically as shorts get squeezed," he said, referring to those holding short positions against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The government and the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of yen buying and dollar selling in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Nikkei newspaper said early Saturday, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Japan's Finance Ministry\uc2  declined to comment on the matter.\par \par \uc2 * "It's clear that the Finance Ministry is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars and yen," said \uc2 Mazen Issa\uc2 , senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  in New York. "They are trying to make a strong case for their expansionary policy."\par \par \uc2 * "A lot of people had considered 150 a key level where they would see some kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and they let it run up to basically 152 and then \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a very illiquid time, when London was about to go home for the weekend. It seems to be designed to inflict as much pain as possible on - they like to use the term - speculators," Issa said.\par \par \uc2 * Earlier on Friday, Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  had said authorities were dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators "sternly," while \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  commented that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would closely monitor the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements.\par \par \uc2 * With Friday's gains, the yen was on track to break a nine-week streak of weekly losses against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 * The dollar index, which measures the strength of the greenback against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was down 0.8% at 112 from a three-week high of 113.95 reached during the session.\par \par \uc2 * The greenback was pressured by a press report that some \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  officials have signaled they are concerned about large interest rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 * The Wall Street Journal reported that Fed officials are headed for another 0.75 percentage point interest rate hike at their November meeting, but that some have begun to signal a desire to slow the pace of hikes soon.\par \par \uc2 (Edited in Spanish by Carlos Serrano and Javier L\u243\'00\'F3pez de L\u233\'00\'E9rida)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221021eial00e08\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
