\par\par \b \uc2 Yen briefly rallies against the dollar as Japanese authorities  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to prop up  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  after hitting 32-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 839 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2022\par 19:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen suddenly rallied against the U.S. dollar on Friday amid reports and widespread speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled to a fresh 32-year low against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the yen had weakened more than 1% against the dollar to as low as 151.95 yen, its lowest level against the dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since July 1990. However, just minutes before the 4 p.m. London \u8220\'20\'1Cfix,\u8221\'20\'1D which is the closest thing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has to a daily close, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair suddenly reversed.\par \par \uc2 However, the yen then strengthened USDJPY, rising more 2% to 147.26 yen to the dollar at its highest level of the session.\par \par \uc2 Market analysts quickly weighed in to say that the move appeared to be the result of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, with some speculating that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be selling U.S. Treasurys or dollars to prop up the yen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt certainly feels like it\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bipan Rai, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at CIBC Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, Japanese news organization Nikkei reported that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had indeed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the falling yen, citing anonymous government officials.\par \par \uc2 Conditions were ripe for Japanese authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Rai said, given the lower liquidity levels on a Friday afternoon and the fact that the dollar was already under pressure following an earlier report in the Wall Street Journal which signaled that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  might downshift to smaller interest-rate hikes after the November policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 The move in the yen comes after the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  carried out unscheduled emergency bond-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday for the second straight day, according to a Reuters report, after the yield on 20-year BX:TMBMKJP-20Yand 30-year BX:TMBMKJP-30YJapanese government bondsBX:TMBMKJP-10Y rose to the highest level since 2015, while the 10-year yield briefly broke above the \uc2 BoJ\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s official ceiling of 25 basis points earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Masato Kanda, Japan\u8217\'20\'19s vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters that Japanese authorities wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t openly announce future \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. He also said that the MoF was \u8220\'20\'1Calways ready to take necessary action as excessive volatility has become increasingly unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The move comes after Japanese core inflation rose to its highest level in eight yearsaccording to data released overnight. On a year-over-year basis, Japan\u8217\'20\'19s core consumer-price index climbed to 3% in September, up from 2.8% the prior month, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 Jon Turek, the founder and CEO of JST Advisors, said Japan\u8217\'20\'19s rising inflation would increase the pressure on the BoJ to compromise on its ultra-loose monetary policy, although he said it would be impossible to anticipate when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might throw in the towel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have a strong view on when they throw in the towel. It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to say considering there\u8217\'20\'19s been no inclination from the BoJ that this could happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Turek said.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Turek said the easiest thing for the MoF to do to prop up the yen would be to sell their massive Treasury holdings.\par \par \uc2 After the latest inflation print, investors will be paying close attention to what BoJ chief \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  might say during next week\u8217\'20\'19s policy meeting, which concludes next Friday. The BoJ is expected to release an update to their macro forecasts after the meeting next week, which could offer some insight into the bank\u8217\'20\'19s thinking, especially the numbers surrounding inflation.\par \par \uc2 There has recently been chatter about the MoF carrying out \u8220\'20\'1Crate checks\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 meaning the ministry has been calling large \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer desks to check the prices on the dollar-yen, Turek said.\par \par \uc2 The strategy has long been used by Japanese authorities to try and move the dollar-yen pair without having to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have repeatedly tried to pressure the BoJ and MoF to capitulate by shorting Japanese government bonds and the yen this year, but so far, Japanese authorities have fended off these speculative attacks by buying more bonds and backstopping the yen when the pace of its decline becomes \u8220\'20\'1Cdisorderly,\u8221\'20\'1D Turek said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not clear that they have a line in the sand at 150 that says \u8216\'20\'18though shall not cross\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Turek said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey just didn\u8217\'20\'19t want the yen to go to 150 in a mess.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the problem with direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is its effects are usually not long-lasting, with market analysts anticipating that the dollar could soon reverse the move, barring more concrete action from the BoJ or the Fed. Indeed the move was already reversing Friday afternoon in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 21, 2022 13:20 ET (17:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020221021eial003je\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
