\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen slides further to 151 per dollar, pound falls on UK turmoil\b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2022\par 13:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Markets on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch as yen tumbles\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pound falls on political uncertainty after PM Truss quits\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dollar demand pushes Swiss franc to lowest since May 2019\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds Swiss franc move, analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 By Iain Withers\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 21 (Reuters) - The yen was on track for its 10th straight weekly decline against the relentlessly strong dollar on Friday, while sterling fell as political turmoil once again gripped Britain.\par \par \uc2 The dollar gained across the board, also pushing the Swiss franc to its lowest level since May 2019.\par \par \uc2 Investor bets on the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  ratcheting up interest rates as high as 5% by next year supported the greenback, as well as company demand for dollars to settle year-end accounts, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index - which tracks the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against six major counterparts - gained 0.5% to 113.440, as \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields climbed to new multi-year peaks.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair is extremely sensitive to changes in U.S. 10-year yields, which pushed to a more than 14-year top of 4.291%.\par \par \uc2 An extended yen sell-off past 150 yen per dollar to 32-year lows has put markets on heightened alert for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Japanese finance minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said on Friday authorities were dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators "strictly", while \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would closely watch the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 The yen last stood at 151.450 per dollar, down 0.9% on the day.\par \par \uc2 "Japan's efforts to highlight that no particular level is being protected means there is scope for this relatively orderly grind higher in USD/JPY to continue," \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts at \uc2 MUFG\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Sterling was also on the back foot, falling more than 1% to a weekly low of $1.11 as Britain's ruling Conservative party began scrambling to pick the country's third prime minister in two months after \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  quit on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had leapt as much as 1% the previous day after Truss announced her departure.\par \par \uc2 The Conservatives, who hold a big majority in parliament and need not call a nationwide election for another two years, will now elect a new leader by Oct. 28. \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  and former finance minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  are the early frontrunners.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell 0.4% to $0.97500, while the Swiss franc fell as much as 1% to a more than three-year low of 1.01230 franc per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  drew more than $11 billion from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap line facility this week, after 17 parties took part in its dollar auction - which analysts said highlighted dollar demand.\par \par \uc2 "There's global demand for dollars, that's also reflected in Switzerland" said \uc2 Kenneth Broux\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 . "Demand for dollars from Swiss institutions has certainly increased."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Iain Withers, additional reporting by Rae Wee and Kevin Buckland; Editing by Alison Williams and Mark Potter) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-21T12:22:42.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221021eial01zrd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
