\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Asian shares lower, yields rise on aggressive rate hike jitters\b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2022\par 04:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 21 (Reuters) - Asian shares tracked Wall Street lower on Friday while Treasury yields scaled 14-year highs as the prospect of aggressive interest rate hikes from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and recession risks soured investor sentiment.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan was down 0.55% but above the two-and-a-half year low it touched on Thursday. Australia's resources-heavy share index lost 0.74%, while Japan's Nikkei opened 0.38% lower.\par \par \uc2 China's stock market opened 0.1% higher on Friday. \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , set to clinch a third five-year term as China's leader, will reveal the members of its elite Politburo Standing Committee at the conclusion of the twice-a-decade congress on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 "It's all so tenuous... the problem is the macro environment still remains difficult," said \uc2 Shane Oliver\uc2 , chief economist at AMP Capital, adding that the market is in a tug of war between investors who see opportunities and those who are focused on the difficult environment.\par \par \uc2 Also weighing on the market were remarks from Philadelphia Federal Reserve President \uc2 Patrick Harker\uc2  that suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will "keep raising rates for a while."\par \par \uc2 U.S. economic data on Thursday showing persistent labor tightness also added to investor angst. U.S. benchmark 10-year Treasury yields to as much as 4.234%, its highest level since June 2008.\par \par \uc2 "It really is the U.S. bond show that drives broad markets and while liquidity is an issue, talk is there are just no buyers," said Chris Weston, head of research at Pepperstone.\par \par \uc2 Global markets have been extremely volatile recently as investors have worried that major economies will be pushed into recessions before inflation is tamed, while a strong dollar as the Fed tightens aggressively would wreak havoc in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, sterling dipped lower as investors digested the news that British Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  had quit after just six weeks in office. The pound was last trading at $1.1205, down 0.25% on the day.\par \par \uc2 Truss' resignation surprised no-one and was met with little market reaction given the wholesale abandonment of her policies by the finance minister, said Tapas Strickland, head of market economics at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen hovered near a fresh 32-year low, and last traded at 150.20 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  first weakened past the symbolic 150 level late Thursday afternoon in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Fresh threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  made by Japanese policymakers have kept investors on high alert, although there has been no news of further action since the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-selling, yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's core consumer inflation rate accelerating to a fresh eight-year high of 3.0% in September, the data underscores the dilemma the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  faces as it tries to underpin a weak economy by maintaining ultra-low interest rates, which in turn are fuelling an unwelcome slide in the yen.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, gold prices were set for a second weekly decline.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ankur Banerjee; Editing by Lincoln Feast) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-21T03:16:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221021eial00af1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
