\par\par \b \uc2 Japanese Yen Hits 150 Per Dollar, a 32-Year Low -- WSJ\b0\par\par\uc2 By Megumi Fujikawa and Chelsey Dulaney \par \uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2022\par 11:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen fell to the lowest level against the dollar since 1990, the latest milestone in the greenback's relentless, once-in-a-generation rally.\par \par \uc2 One dollar briefly bought just over 150 yen on Thursday, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2  data, breaching a level seen as important by investors and economists. The dollar eased slightly in mid-morning trade in London, with one greenback recently buying 149.95 yen.\par \par \uc2 Propelled by a hawkish \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and the U.S.'s relative economic strength, the dollar has soared against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the euro, pound and Chinese yuan. But Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under particular stress because its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains uniquely committed to keeping interest rates ultralow.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  conducted unscheduled bond buying to bring down bond yields. That came after the 10-year government bond yield exceeded its 0.25% ceiling, as set out in a policy known as yield-curve control ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bank-of-japan-can-stomach-weak-yen-11662643391"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/bank-of-\b  \highlight22japan\b0 \highlight22 -can-stomach-weak-yen-11662643391}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/japan-intervenes-in-currency-market-to-support-yen-11663836942"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/\b  \highlight22japan\b0 \highlight22 -\b  \highlight22intervenes\b0 \highlight22 -in-\b  \highlight22currency\b0 \highlight22 -market-to-support-yen-11663836942}}}\uc2 ) last month to defend the yen, but that hasn't stopped its decline. Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  has warned the government could act again. "We will take appropriate action decisively against any excessive moves" in the yen, Mr. Suzuki has repeatedly said this week.\par \par \uc2 NOTE: In-line links reference additional content of interest chosen by the WSJ news team.\par \par \uc2 This item is part of a Wall Street Journal live coverage event. The full stream can be found by searching P/WSJL (WSJ Live Coverage).\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 20, 2022 05:36 ET (09:36 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020221020eiak001y8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
