\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 -dollar rises to 150 yen threshold; pound rises on truss resignation\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 (.)\par \par \uc2 By Karen Brettell\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 20 (Reuters) - The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated on Thursday to touch the psychological level of 150 yen for the first time since 1990, while sterling rose as \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  announced her resignation as British prime minister.\par \par \uc2 * The fragile yen briefly surpassed 150 yen to the dollar for the first time since August 1990. In late trading, it was trading at 149.76 units.\par \par \uc2 * The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply from a high of 150.09 to 149.63 within a minute, reigniting speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are making stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at key levels.\par \par \uc2 * However, some analysts believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially smaller ones, may not stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening further without a change in the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's ultra-loose policy.\par \par \uc2 * "Until the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  changes its tune, or if we start to see the U.S. economic outlook deteriorate much faster, which would help the Fed to finally pivot, we will see betting against the yen remain the favored trade in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said \uc2 Edward Moya\uc2 , senior market analyst at \uc2 OANDA\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 * This has pushed U.S. bond yields and the dollar higher, especially against the yen, as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  has pledged to keep rates near zero.\par \par \uc2 * The pound rose after \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  announced her resignation, brought down by her economic program that rattled markets and divided her Conservative Party just six weeks after her appointment. In its latest trading, it was up 0.78% at $1.1311.\par \par \uc2 * The dollar index was off 0.5% at 112.40 and the euro was up 0.46% at $0.9817.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Alun John and Samuel Indyk in London; edited in Spanish by Javier L\u243\'00\'F3pez de L\u233\'00\'E9rida and Carlos Serrano).\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221021eiak002rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
