\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen hits weakest level since 1990, pound down after PM announces resignation\b0\par\par\uc2 995 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2022\par 21:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds data, comments from Fed's Harker, updates prices)\par \par         * \par       Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par   \par     By Karen Brettell\par        NEW YORK, Oct 20 (Reuters) - The dollar surpassed the\par symbolic level of 150 yen for the first time since 1990 on\par Thursday, while the British pound turned negative in choppy\par trading after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liz Truss\f28 \uc2 \f2  said she would resign as the United\par Kingdom's prime minister.\par     The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dipped sharply from an interim high of\par 150.09 reached in overnight trading, tumbling to 149.63 within a\par minute, which raised speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par and Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might be making stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at key\par levels.\par     The yen rebounded to hit new 32-year highs in\par afternoon trading in New York, however, getting as high as\par 150.25. It last traded at 150.18. \par     While the likelihood of any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is an open\par question, some analysts think that such a move would not stop\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from weakening further absent a shift in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's ultra-dovish policy.\par     "Until you see either the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  change their tune, or if we\par start to see the U.S. economic outlook deteriorate a lot quicker\par that will help the Fed finally deliver that Fed pivot, you're\par going to see that the bet against the yen is still the favorite\par trade in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Edward Moya\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior market analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 OANDA\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par in New York.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to continue raising interest\par rates as inflation remains stubbornly high, with some\par forecasting its benchmark overnight interest rate to peak above\par 5%. The rate is currently in the 3.00%-3.25% range.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philadelphia Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Patrick Harker\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Thursday\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not done with raising its short-term rate\par target amid very high levels of inflation, while adding it was\par likely the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will find space next year to pause\par the tightening process and take stock of how its rate increases\par are impacting the economy.\par     The housing market has been one of the most affected sectors\par from higher rates even as other sectors including jobs remain\par solid. Data on Thursday showed that sales of existing U.S. homes\par slid for an eighth straight month in September.\par     Expectations of higher rates have sent U.S. yields and the\par dollar higher, particularly against the yen as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  is\par committed to keeping interest rates near zero.\par     Japanese policymakers made fresh threats of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Thursday. They are seen as more likely to step in if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par moves become more erratic.\par     "The (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) has been very clear that they are\par ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if there is any disorderly price action, so\par the markets are priced for that coming at some point in time,"\par said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Derek Halpenny\f28 \uc2 \f2 , European global markets research head at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 MUFG\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Obviously, if we break clearly above 150 we may see some\par disorderly price action and that could be the catalyst for some\par action," he added, though emphasizing it would take a sharp move\par in the pair to trigger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  will hold its next policy meeting on Oct. 27-28.\par     The British pound turned lower on the day after Truss said\par she would resign as prime minister. She was brought down by the\par announcement of an economic program that sent shockwaves through\par the markets and divided her Conservative Party just six weeks\par after she was appointed.\par     The pound rallied ahead of the resignation announcement, and\par later hit session highs, before changing course and turning\par lower. It was last down 0.05% on the day at $1.1219.\par     "Initially, this is likely to take an uncertainty premium\par out of the market, but it depends who takes over, you need a\par steady hand at the top," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Viraj Patel\f28 \uc2 \f2 , global macro\par strategist at Vanda Research in London.\par     The dollar index dipped 0.10% against a basket of major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to 112.86, which analysts said was likely due\par to consolidation. The euro gained 0.13% to $0.9785.\par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b