\par\par \b \uc2 Yen hits weakest level since 1990, pound down after PM announces resignation\b0\par\par\uc2 972 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2022\par 22:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The dollar surpassed the symbolic level of 150 yen for the first time since 1990 on Thursday, while the British pound turned negative in choppy trading after \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  said she would resign as the United Kingdom's prime minister.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped sharply from an interim high of 150.09 reached in overnight trading, tumbling to 149.63 within a minute, which raised speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be making stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at key levels.\par \par \uc2 The yen rebounded to hit new 32-year highs in afternoon trading in New York, however, getting as high as 150.25. It last traded at 150.18.\par \par \uc2 While the likelihood of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an open question, some analysts think that such a move would not stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening further absent a shift in the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's ultra-dovish policy.\par \par \uc2 "Until you see either the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  change their tune, or if we start to see the U.S. economic outlook deteriorate a lot quicker that will help the Fed finally deliver that Fed pivot, you're going to see that the bet against the yen is still the favorite trade in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \uc2 Edward Moya\uc2 , senior market analyst at \uc2 OANDA\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is expected to continue raising interest rates as inflation remains stubbornly high, with some forecasting its benchmark overnight interest rate to peak above 5%. The rate is currently in the 3.00%-3.25% range.\par \par \uc2 Philadelphia Fed\uc2  President \uc2 Patrick Harker\uc2  said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not done with raising its short-term rate target amid very high levels of inflation, while adding it was likely the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will find space next year to pause the tightening process and take stock of how its rate increases are impacting the economy.\par \par \uc2 The housing market has been one of the most affected sectors from higher rates even as other sectors including jobs remain solid. Data on Thursday showed that sales of existing U.S. homes slid for an eighth straight month in September.\par \par \uc2 Expectations of higher rates have sent U.S. yields and the dollar higher, particularly against the yen as the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is committed to keeping interest rates near zero.\par \par \uc2 Japanese policymakers made fresh threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. They are seen as more likely to step in if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves become more erratic.\par \par \uc2 "The (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has been very clear that they are ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is any disorderly price action, so the markets are priced for that coming at some point in time," said \uc2 Derek Halpenny\uc2 , European global markets research head at \uc2 MUFG\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Obviously, if we break clearly above 150 we may see some disorderly price action and that could be the catalyst for some action," he added, though emphasizing it would take a sharp move in the pair to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will hold its next policy meeting on Oct. 27-28.\par \par \uc2 The British pound turned lower on the day after Truss said she would resign as prime minister. She was brought down by the announcement of an economic program that sent shockwaves through the markets and divided her Conservative Party just six weeks after she was appointed.\par \par \uc2 The pound rallied ahead of the resignation announcement, and later hit session highs, before changing course and turning lower. It was last down 0.05% on the day at $1.1219.\par \par \uc2 "Initially, this is likely to take an uncertainty premium out of the market, but it depends who takes over, you need a steady hand at the top," said \uc2 Viraj Patel\uc2 , global macro strategist at Vanda Research in London.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index dipped 0.10% against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 112.86, which analysts said was likely due to consolidation. The euro gained 0.13% to $0.9785.\par \par \uc2 ========================================================\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 3:03PM (1903 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Description RIC Last U.S. Close Pct Change YTD Pct High Bid Low Bid\par \par \uc2 Previous Change\par \par \uc2 Session\par \par \uc2 Dollar index 112.8600 112.9800 -0.10% 17.977% +113.0900 +112.1600\par \par \uc2 Euro/Dollar $0.9785 $0.9772 +0.13% +0.00% +$0.9846 +$0.9755\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Yen 150.1800 149.9100 +0.19% +0.00% +150.2400 +149.5500\par \par \uc2 Euro/Yen 146.95 146.49 +0.31% +0.00% +147.2900 +146.2500\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Swiss 1.0041 1.0046 -0.04% +0.00% +1.0068 +0.9996\par \par \uc2 Sterling/Dollar $1.1219 $1.1223 -0.05% +0.00% +$1.1336 +$1.1172\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Canadian 1.3769 1.3762 +0.06% +0.00% +1.3806 +1.3651\par \par \uc2 Aussie/Dollar $0.6279 $0.6271 +0.15% +0.00% +$0.6356 +$0.6229\par \par \uc2 Euro/Swiss 0.9826 0.9816 +0.10% +0.00% +0.9851 +0.9812\par \par \uc2 Euro/Sterling 0.8719 0.8710 +0.10% +0.00% +0.8757 +0.8675\par \par \uc2 NZ $0.5674 $0.5677 -0.03% +0.00% +$0.5741 +$0.5