\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Traders on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  watch as yen hits 150, pound gains as Truss resigns\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2022\par 16:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds quotes, details; updates prices; changes byline,\par dateline; previous LONDON)\par \par         * \par       Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par   \par     By Karen Brettell\par        NEW YORK, Oct 20 (Reuters) - The dollar hit the symbolic\par level of 150 yen for the first time since 1990 on Thursday,\par while the British pound rose as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liz Truss\f28 \uc2 \f2  said she would resign\par as prime minister.\par     The fragile yen briefly weakened past 150 per\par dollar for the first time since August 1990. It was last trading\par at 149.76 yen per dollar.\par     The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sharply dipped from a high of 150.09,\par tumbling to 149.63 within a minute, which has again raised\par speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might\par be making stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at key levels.\par     However, some analysts think that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially\par small ones, may not stop the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from weakening further\par absent a shift in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 \u8217\'20\'19s ultra-dovish policy.\par     \u8220\'20\'1CUntil you see either the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  change their tune, or if we\par start to see the U.S. economic outlook deteriorate a lot quicker\par that will help the Fed finally deliver that Fed pivot, you\u8217\'20\'19re\par going to see that the bet against the yen is still the favorite\par trade in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Edward Moya\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior market anlayst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 OANDA\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par in New York.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to continue raising interest\par rates as inflation remains stubbornly high, with some\par forecasting a peak above 5%.\par     This has sent U.S. yields and the dollar higher,\par particularly against the yen as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  is committed\par to keeping interest rates near zero.\par     Japanese policymakers made fresh threats of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Thursday. They are seen as more likely to step in if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par moves become more erratic.\par     "The (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) has been very clear that they are\par ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if there is any disorderly price action, so\par the markets are priced for that coming at some point in time,"\par said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Derek Halpenny\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of research, global markets EMEA at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 MUFG\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Obviously, if we break clearly above 150 we may see some\par disorderly price action and that could be the catalyst for some\par action," he added, though emphasizing it would take a sharp move\par in the pair to trigger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  will hold its next policy meeting on Oct. 27-28.\par     The British pound was higher on the day after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liz Truss\f28 \uc2 \f2  said\par she would resign as prime minister, brought down by her economic\par program that sent shockwaves through the markets and divided her\par Conservative Party just six weeks after she was appointed.\par     "Initially, this is likely to take an uncertainty premium\par out of the market but it depends who takes over, you need a\par steady hand at the top," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Viraj Patel\f28 \uc2 \f2 , global macro\par strategist at Vanda Research in London.\par     The pound rallied ahead of the announcement, before paring\par gains and then again moving higher. It was last up 63%\par on the day at $1.1293.\par     The dollar index dipped 0.50% against a basket of major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to 112.40, which analysts said was likely due\par to consolidation. The euro gained 0.46% to $0.9817.\par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:17AM (1417 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 112.4000       112.9800    -0.50%         17.496%       +113.0900   +112.2700\par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9817        $0.9772     +0.46%         -13.65%       +$0.9837    +$0.9755\par  Dollar/Yen                   149.7600       149.9100    -0.10%         +30.10%       +150.0700   +149.6300\par  Euro/Yen                     147.02         146.49      +0.36%         +12.81%       +147.2500   +146.2500\par  Dollar/Swiss                 1.0016         1.0046      -0.27%         +9.84%        +1.0068  