\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen weakens past 150 per dollar for first time in 32 years\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2022\par 10:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE/LONDON, Oct 20 (Reuters) - The dollar hit the symbolic level of 150 yen on Thursday as the greenback was supported by Treasury yields trading at multi-year highs, keeping markets on high alert for any signs of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese authorities.\par \par \uc2 Moves among other majors were more muted with the euro at $0.97835 and sterling at $1.1217, both failing to regain ground on the dollar, after tumbling the day before.\par \par \uc2 The fragile yen briefly weakened past 150 per dollar in early European trading for the first time since August 1990. It was last trading flat a little below that level.\par \par \uc2 It has been on a losing streak for 11 straight sessions as of Wednesday's close, and has renewed 32-year lows for six sessions now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a big psychological level that could trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 people have been anticipating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a while,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sim Moh Siong, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Bank of Singapore\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are going to look over their shoulders for a while and see whether there\u8217\'20\'19s any action or not, if not, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to push it further, higher. That\u8217\'20\'19s how the market goes. The next resistance I see would be around 153 level.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last month, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy yen for the first time since 1998 in an attempt to shore up the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weakening as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to keep Japanese benchmark yields pinned near zero, at a time when those elsewhere are rising.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rose to 4.18% on Thursday, its highest level since mid-2008, while the two-year Treasury yields touched a 15-year high of 4.6079%.\par \par \uc2 U.S. yields have been driven higher as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  looks set to continue with its aggressive pace of interest rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 Overnight, Fed officials also continued their hawkish rhetoric, as \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Minneapolis\uc2  President \uc2 Neel Kashkari\uc2  said that U.S. job market demand remains strong and underlying inflation pressures probably have not peaked yet.\par \par \uc2 The euro climbed a whisker on the pound but the British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely ignored the latest political turmoil in the United Kingdom, with the departure of the interior minister being the latest matter to add to the uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 The surging greenback also pushed the Chinese offshore yuan to a record low in Asia of 7.2794 early in the session, its weakest level since such data first became available in 2011.\par \par \uc2 It later trimmed intraday losses on a \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  report China is considering a cut in the duration of quarantine for inbound visitors from 10 days to seven days.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Rae Wee and Alun John; Editing by Stephen Coates and Angus MacSwan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-20T09:06:40.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221020eiak01f8i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
