\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar gains with Treasury yields, sterling tumbles on hot inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 994 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2022\par 21:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds comments from Fed's Kashkari, Beige Book, quotes, updates\par prices)\par \par         * \par       Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par   \par     By Karen Brettell\par        NEW YORK, Oct 19 (Reuters) - The dollar bounced from\par two-week lows on Wednesday as benchmark 10-year Treasury yields\par rose to 14-year highs, while sterling weakened after\par hotter-than-expected UK consumer price inflation fueled concerns\par about a deeper recession.\par     The greenback hit a 32-year peak against the yen,\par approaching the 150 level at which some traders think the Bank\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Treasury yields resumed their march higher as\par investors maintained expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will\par continue to aggressively raise interest rates to bring down\par soaring inflation, boosting demand for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to lift rates by another\par 75 basis points when it meets on November 1-2, with an\par additional 50 or 75 basis point increase also likely in\par December.\par     It is "still very much premature to try to fade the dollar,"\par said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mazen Issa\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD\par Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It will likely continue to gain until momentum in\par core inflation moderates and the Fed pivots to a less hawkish\par stance, and "neither are likely in the short term".\par     Fed Bank of Minneapolis President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Neel Kashkari\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on\par Wednesday that job market demand remained strong and underlying\par inflation pressures probably had not peaked yet.\par     The Fed's Beige Book on Wednesday showed that U.S. economic\par activity expanded modestly in recent weeks, although it was flat\par in some regions and declined in a couple of others, in a report\par that showed firms growing more pessimistic about the outlook.\par     The dollar index gained 0.88% against a basket of major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to 112.92. The euro fell 0.95% to\par $0.9771.\par     The British pound fell 1.02% to $1.1210 after data\par showed that Britain's annual consumer price inflation inched up\par to 10.1% in September, rising more than expected and returning\par to a 40-year high hit in July.\par     "The outlook for the UK economy remains relatively murky,\par with ballooning borrowing costs, soaring consumer prices and a\par government in chaos with its credibility shot to bits unlikely\par to inspire much confidence," said Matthew Ryan, head of market\par strategy at Ebury.\par     Investors expect sterling to remain under pressure amid an\par outlook for rising inflation and a recession in Britain which\par could lead the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  to increase rates by 75 basis\par points rather than 100 bps at its November meeting.\par     While interest rate hikes would normally boost a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par in the case of the United Kingdom the focus is on the degree to\par which they will harm the already precarious economy.\par     "The economy is going to suffer and so that means that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is going to have to be the release valve to reflect\par that shift in the outlook on the macro side," said Issa. \par     YEN WATCH\par     The dollar was last 0.43% up on the day at 149.87 yen\par .\par     Traders are on high alert for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  and\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step into the market again, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par pair pushes toward the key psychological barrier at 150. A cross\par of 145 a month ago spurred the first yen-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par since 1998 to prop up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Japanese Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday\par that he was checking \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates "meticulously" and with more\par frequency, local media reported.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains an outlier among a global wave of central\par banks tightening monetary policy to combat soaring inflation, as\par it focuses on underpinning a fragile economy.\par     Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  said that the yen could weaken\par beyond 150 if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  maintains this outlook\par at its meeting on Oct. 27-28.\par     "We are open to fresh surges higher if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  stands pat at\par its meeting this month, with minimal respect for the capacity of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to compress movement," analysts led by Shahab\par Jalinoos said in a report sent on Tuesday.\par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 3:09PM (1909 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 112.9200       111.9600    +0.88%         18.039%       +113.0900   +111.9200\par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9771        $0.9861     -0.95%         -14.09%       +$0.9873    +$0.9758\par  Dollar/Yen                   149.8700       149.2350    +0.43%         +30.19%       +149.8850   +149.1000\par  Euro/Yen                     146.45         147.09      -0.44%         +12.38%       +147.2500   +146.1000\par  Dollar/Swiss                 1.0049         0.9940      +1.15%         +10.22%       +1.0062     +0.9929\par  Sterling/Dollar              $1.1210        $1.1319     -1.02%         -17.16%       +$1.1356    +$1.1186\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.3777         1.3736      +0.32%         +8.99%        +1.3809     +1.3720\par  Aussie/Dollar                $0.6263        $0.6310     -0.74%         -13.85%       +$0.6325    +$0.6253\par  Euro/Swiss                   0.9819         0.9803      +0.16%         -5.30%        +0.9830     +0.9791\par  Euro/Sterling                0.8715         0.8704      +0.13%         +3.75%        +0.8729     +0.8682\par  NZ                           $0.5664        $0.5686     -0.40%         -17.26%       +$0.5707    +$0.5650\par  Dollar/Dollar                                                                                    \par  Dollar/Norway                10.6285        10.5640     +0.64%         +20.68%       +10.6560    +10.5675\par  Euro/Norway                 