\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar gains with Treasury yields, sterling tumbles on hot inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 969 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2022\par 21:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The dollar bounced from two-week lows on Wednesday as benchmark 10-year Treasury yields rose to 14-year highs, while sterling weakened after hotter-than-expected UK consumer price inflation fueled concerns about a deeper recession.\par \par \uc2 The greenback hit a 32-year peak against the yen, approaching the 150 level at which some traders think the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Treasury yields resumed their march higher as investors maintained expectations that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will continue to aggressively raise interest rates to bring down soaring inflation, boosting demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to lift rates by another 75 basis points when it meets on November 1-2, with an additional 50 or 75 basis point increase also likely in December.\par \par \uc2 It is "still very much premature to try to fade the dollar," said \uc2 Mazen Issa\uc2 , senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 . It will likely continue to gain until momentum in core inflation moderates and the Fed pivots to a less hawkish stance, and "neither are likely in the short term".\par \par \uc2 Fed Bank of Minneapolis President \uc2 Neel Kashkari\uc2  said on Wednesday that job market demand remained strong and underlying inflation pressures probably had not peaked yet.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's Beige Book on Wednesday showed that U.S. economic activity expanded modestly in recent weeks, although it was flat in some regions and declined in a couple of others, in a report that showed firms growing more pessimistic about the outlook.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index gained 0.88% against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 112.92. The euro fell 0.95% to $0.9771.\par \par \uc2 The British pound fell 1.02% to $1.1210 after data showed that Britain's annual consumer price inflation inched up to 10.1% in September, rising more than expected and returning to a 40-year high hit in July.\par \par \uc2 "The outlook for the UK economy remains relatively murky, with ballooning borrowing costs, soaring consumer prices and a government in chaos with its credibility shot to bits unlikely to inspire much confidence," said Matthew Ryan, head of market strategy at Ebury.\par \par \uc2 Investors expect sterling to remain under pressure amid an outlook for rising inflation and a recession in Britain which could lead the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  to increase rates by 75 basis points rather than 100 bps at its November meeting.\par \par \uc2 While interest rate hikes would normally boost a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in the case of the United Kingdom the focus is on the degree to which they will harm the already precarious economy.\par \par \uc2 "The economy is going to suffer and so that means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to have to be the release valve to reflect that shift in the outlook on the macro side," said Issa.\par \par \uc2 YEN WATCH\par \par \uc2 The dollar was last 0.43% up on the day at 149.87 yen.\par \par \uc2 Traders are on high alert for \uc2 Japan's finance ministry\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step into the market again, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair pushes toward the key psychological barrier at 150. A cross of 145 a month ago spurred the first yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998 to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said on Wednesday that he was checking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates "meticulously" and with more frequency, local media reported.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  remains an outlier among a global wave of central banks tightening monetary policy to combat soaring inflation, as it focuses on underpinning a fragile economy.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  said that the yen could weaken beyond 150 if the \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains this outlook at its meeting on Oct. 27-28.\par \par \uc2 "We are open to fresh surges higher if the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  stands pat at its meeting this month, with minimal respect for the capacity of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to compress movement," analysts led by Shahab Jalinoos said in a report sent on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ========================================================\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 3:09PM (1909 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Description RIC Last U.S. Close Pct Change YTD Pct High Bid Low Bid\par \par \uc2 Previous Change\par \par \uc2 Session\par \par \uc2 Dollar index 112.9200 111.9600 +0.88% 18.039% +113.0900 +111.9200\par \par \uc2 Euro/Dollar $0.9771 $0.9861 -0.95% -14.09% +$0.9873 +$0.9758\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Yen 149.8700 149.2350 +0.43% +30.19% +149.8850 +149.1000\par \par \uc2 Euro/Yen 146.45 147.09 -0.44% +12.38% +147.2500 +146.1000\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Swiss 1.0049 0.9940 +1.15% +10.22% +1.0062 +0.9929\par \par \uc2 Sterling/Dollar $1.1210 $1.1319 -1.02% -17.16% +$1.1356 +$1.1186\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Canadian 1.3777 1.3736 +0.32% +8.99% +1.3809 +1.3720\par \par \uc2 Aussie/Dollar $0.6263 $0.6310 -0.74% -13.85% +$0.6325 +$0.6253\par \par \uc2 Euro/Swiss 0.9819 0.9803 +0