\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar gains with Treasury yields, sterling tumbles on hot inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 875 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2022\par 16:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds quotes, details; updates prices; changes byline,\par dateline; previous LONDON)\par \par         * \par       Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par   \par     By Karen Brettell\par        NEW YORK, Oct 19 (Reuters) - The dollar bounced from\par two-week lows on Wednesday as Treasury yields rose to 14-year\par highs, while sterling weakened after hotter-than-expected UK\par consumer price inflation and fears of a deeper recession in\par Britain bolstered expectations of a less aggressive rate hike by\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 BoE\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) in November.\par     The greenback also hit a 32-year peak against the yen and\par approached the 150 level where some traders think the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the tumbling\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Benchmark 10-year Treasury yields resumed their\par march higher as investors maintained expectations that the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will continue to aggressively raise rates to\par bring down soaring inflation, boosting demand for the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to lift rates by another\par 75 basis points when it meets on November 1-2, with an\par additional 50 basis points or 75 basis points increase also\par likely in December.\par     It is \u8220\'20\'1Cstill very much premature to try to fade the dollar,\u8221\'20\'1D\par said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mazen Issa\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD\par Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The greenback will likely continue to gain until\par momentum in core inflation moderates and the Fed pivots to a\par less hawkish stance, and \u8220\'20\'1Cneither are likely in the short term\u8221\'20\'1D.\par     The dollar index gained 0.73% against a basket of major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  <=USD< to 112.76. The euro fell 0.80% to\par $0.9782.\par     The British pound fell 0.61% to $1.1249 after data\par showed that Britain's annual consumer price inflation inched up\par to 10.1% in September, rising more than expected and returning\par to a 40-year high hit in July.\par     "The outlook for the UK economy remains relatively murky,\par with ballooning borrowing costs, soaring consumer prices and a\par government in chaos with its credibility shot to bits unlikely\par to inspire much confidence," said Matthew Ryan, head of market\par strategy at Ebury.\par     Investors expect sterling to remain under pressure amid an\par outlook for rising inflation and a recession in Britain which\par could lead the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BoE\f28 \uc2 \f2  to increase rates by 75 basis points rather\par than 100 bps at its November meeting.\par     While interest rate hikes would normally boost a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par in the case of the United Kingdom the focus is on the degree to\par which they will harm the already precarious economy.\par     \u8220\'20\'1CThe economy is going to suffer and so that means that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is going to have to be the release valve to reflect\par that shift in the outlook on the macro side,\u8221\'20\'1D said Issa. \par     YEN WATCH\par     The dollar was last 0.32% up on the day at 149.71 yen\par .\par     Traders are on high alert for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  and\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step into the market again, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par pair pushes toward the key psychological barrier at 150. A cross\par of 145 a month ago spurred the first yen-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par since 1998 to prop up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Japanese Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday\par that he was checking \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates "meticulously" and with more\par frequency, local media reported.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains an outlier among a global wave of central\par banks tightening monetary policy to combat soaring inflation, as\par it focuses on underpinning a fragile economy.\par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:14AM (1414 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 112.7600       111.9600    +0.73%         17.872%       +112.9800   +111.9200\par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9782        $0