\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Asia stocks, pound savour the relief of UK U-turn\b0\par\par\uc2 642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2022\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 18 (Reuters) - Asia stocks rose on Tuesday as the dramatic U-turn in British fiscal policy brightened investor sentiment, while sterling flirted with two-weeks high on hopes the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  may further delay plans for quantitative tightening.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan was up 1.55%, while Japan's Nikkei rose 1.59%.\par \par \uc2 European stock futures indicated stocks were set to continue their ascent, with the Eurostoxx 50 futures up 1.25%, German DAX futures up 1.22% and FTSE futures up 0.87%. U.S. futures also pointed to a higher opening with S&P 500 futures up 1.6% and Nasdaq futures up 1.8%.\par \par \uc2 The British \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had already delayed the start of a scheme to sell down 838 billion pounds ($954.90 billion) of government bond holdings, is likely to push the sale of the bonds, the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  reported on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The FT report comes a day after Britain's new finance minister \uc2 Jeremy Hunt\uc2  abandoned most of Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 ' economic plan that had led to a political maelstrom fuelled by market turmoil, resulting in the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  being forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to calm the bond market.\par \par \uc2 Sterling was last trading at $1.1382, up 0.26% on the day, adding to its gains of 1.6% in the previous session. The pound had jumped 0.36% to $1.1398, near Monday's high of $1.144, the strongest since Oct. 5.\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  analysts said the fiscal U-turn was likely to have significant implications for the \uc2 BoE\uc2  as its economists now revise their call for the November meeting to a 75-basis-point rate hike, from 100 basis points.\par \par \uc2 "Given such a wholesale scrapping of Truss' Tory leadership promises, it remains an open question how long Truss will remain in power," said Tapas Strickland, head of market economics at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 China's stock market nudged higher, up 0.2% as the Chinese ruling Communist Party's twice-a-decade congress remains in session this week.\par \par \uc2 Chinese state banks are stepping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the weakening yuan, banking sources told Reuters on Monday, while many companies have announced share buyback programmes.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index fell 0.178%, touching its lowest levels since Oct. 6, while the euro was up 0.21% to $0.9859.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar rose on Tuesday after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  said it expects to raise interest rates further over the coming months.\par \par \uc2 The yen touched a fresh 32-year low of 149.10 per dollar on Monday, not far off the psychological metric of 150.\par \par \uc2 Investors have been watching out for any signs of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with authorities repeatedly warning of a firm response to overly rapid yen declines.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more about speed of moves than it is levels, said \uc2 Ray Attrill\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I don't think the Japanese authorities are particularly keen to see dollar yen at 150 in the immediate term and that's why markets are being a bit guarded."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, China has delayed the release of economic indicators, including the country's third-quarter gross domestic product due on Tuesday and trade data that had been scheduled last Friday.\par \par \uc2 The drop in the dollar helped prop up gold as well as oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude futures rose 74 cents, or 0.8%, to $92.36 per barrel by 0505 GMT, while U.S. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude futures gained 78 cents, or 0.9%, to $86.24 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold was up 0.2% at $1,651.75 per ounce.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jacqueline Wong) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-18T07:13:37.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221018eiai00t39\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
