\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  repeats warnings on yen as market watches for  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2022\par 07:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Yen hits fresh 32-year low beyond 149 to dollar despite warnings\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Finmin says cannot tolerate excessive, speculative yen moves\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducting 'stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 '\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kuroda says few people expect prolonged dollar strength\par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 BOJ\uc2  reserves data)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto and Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 18 (Reuters) - Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  warned on Tuesday that Japan would take appropriate and decisive action against excessive, speculator-driven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, keeping alive the possibility of more market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yen hit a new 32-year low.\par \par \uc2 Suzuki also reiterated that the authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  without any announcements, but did not comment on whether they had actually done so, when pressed on speculation that Japan may be supporting the yen without publicly acknowledging it.\par \par \uc2 "We are closely watching market moves with a high sense of urgency. We will make an appropriate response decisively to excessive moves," Suzuki told a session of parliament on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Pressed by an opposition lawmaker on what a decisive response would mean, he added: "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as a decisive measure (on September 22\u8334\'20\'8E."\par \par \uc2 Suzuki, speaking to reporters earlier on Tuesday, declined to comment whether authorities were conducting stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the weakening yen.\par \par \uc2 "Generally speaking, there are times when we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by making announcements and some other times when we do without it," he said, reiterating comments last week after meetings of financial leaders in Washington. He did not comment further on the matter.\par \par \uc2 The yen slipped to 149.10 to the dollar before the start of Asia trade on Tuesday, its weakest since August 1990, putting the major psychological barrier of 150 in focus.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers, who once zeroed in on yen strength as a source of concern for the trade-oriented economy, are now worried that the yen's sharp fall is boosting already high commodity import costs, squeezing households, and upending business plans.\par \par \uc2 Authorities have fired verbal warnings against the yen's descent almost daily since early September, when it reached 144 to the dollar as rate hikes by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  boosted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Suzuki first acknowledged yen weakness as negative for the economy in April, when it was trading around 126 per dollar. It has continued to fall sharply and is down about 20% since the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 Japan spent 2.8 trillion yen ($18.81 billion) in dollar-selling, yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month when authorities acted in the markets to prop up the yen for the first time since 1998.\par \par \uc2 Estimates by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  released last Friday showed that excess reserves parked by institutions at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely have declined 4.09 trillion yen as of Monday, Oct. 17, due in part to actions that could be related to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's previous estimate, released on Sept. 30, indicated a decline of 2.9 trillion yen as of the start of October.\par \par \uc2 The gap of more than 1 trillion yen could reflect funds absorbed from excess reserves as a result of yen-buying, dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This has fuelled speculation among market players that the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market without announcing it.\par \par \uc2 At Tuesday's parliamentary session, Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2  joined in warning that rapid, speculation-driven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were problematic.\par \par \uc2 Kishida brushed aside the dominant market view that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's ultra-easy monetary policy was largely behind the yen's sharp declines, saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates move on various factors, not just on U.S.-Japan interest rate differentials.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  decides monetary policy based not just on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves but comprehensive factors, such as economic and price developments as well as the impact on small and midsize firms," Kishida said.\par \par \uc2 Kuroda, who was also appearing in parliament after attending last week's meetings of global financial leaders, suggested that the dollar's strength may not persist.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar has become very strong against all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world," Kuroda said. "But few of the people I met in Washington were thinking that it would last long." ($1 = 148.8400 yen) (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Additional reporting by Daniel Leussink; Editing by Kim Coghill, Sam Holmes and Edmund Klamann) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-18T06:45:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221018eiai0030d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
