\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar tests 32-year peak to yen; Aussie, kiwi rise on rate bets\b0\par\par\uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2022\par 03:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 18 (Reuters) - The dollar hovered near a 32-year peak above 149 yen on Tuesday even as it took a breather from a rally against other major peers, with traders bracing for possible further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Aussie strengthened after minutes from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 's last meeting showed the decision to slow the pace of rate hikes to a quarter point instead of delivering another half point increase was "finely balanced."\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar surged after a hotter-than-expected consumer price report boosted expectations for further policy tightening.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 148.855 yen after pushing to 149.10 late in the overnight session for the first time since August 1990. That puts the major psychological barrier of 150 in focus.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the U.S. dollar index - which measures the greenback against six major peers, including the yen, euro and sterling - sagged near a 1-1/2-week low as a dramatic U-turn over the UK's controversial tax-slashing "mini-budget" buoyed European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar-yen pair has strengthened 3% since Oct. 5, when it sustainably broke above 145 after spending about two weeks hovering near that level, hemmed in by trader nerves following the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998 on Sept. 22.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  admitted following the recent \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  gathering that "there wasn't any discussion on what coordinated steps could be taken" about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  has also made clear that Washington had no appetite for concerted action, saying the dollar's overall strength was a "natural result of different paces of monetary tightening in the United States and other countries."\par \par \uc2 Closing on 150 though, the risk of unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese authorities is a worry for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, although its success may be limited, according to Shinichiro Kadota, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in Tokyo\par \par \uc2 "If the market continues to march higher, especially with some volatility, the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  definitely increases," Kadota said.\par \par \uc2 "But at the end of the day, it's really being driven by broad dollar strength and Fed hiking expectations. As long as that is there, then upward pressure on dollar-yen remains."\par \par \uc2 Absent the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo, Kadota said the dollar should already be above 150 yen based on interest-rate differentials and other market factors.\par \par \uc2 A red-hot U.S. consumer inflation report last week boosted bets for even more aggressive U.S. policy tightening, with markets currently priced for 75 basis point hikes in November and December.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, sterling eased a touch to $1.1349 after surging 1.6% on Monday and touching $1.144 for the first time since Oct. 5.\par \par \uc2 Jeremy Hunt, who was appointed finance minister by Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  on Friday, reversed swathes of the 45-billion pound "mini-budget" that sparked market turmoil, sent the pound crashing to record lows and forced the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a bond market rout.\par \par \uc2 The euro was flat at $0.9838 after earlier touching the highest since Oct. 6 at $0.9853.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar rose 0.14% to $0.630, supported after minutes from the \uc2 RBA\uc2 's Oct. 4 meeting showed the surprise decision to slow the pace of policy tightening was "finely balanced." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor \uc2 Michele Bullock\uc2  said in a speech on Tuesday that the \uc2 RBA\uc2  can keep pace with tightening by global peers.\par \par \uc2 New Zealand's kiwi jumped 0.57% to $0.567 after a report showed consumer inflation continued to hover near three-decade highs in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Buckland Editing by Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-18T02:53:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221018eiai008c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
