\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar dips as UK budget U-turn improves market sentiment\b0\par\par\uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2022\par 21:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds quotes, details; updates prices.)\par \par         * \par       Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par   \par     By Karen Brettell\par        NEW YORK, Oct 17 (Reuters) - The dollar dipped against a\par basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and sterling jumped on Monday after\par Britain's new finance minister ditched most of the government's\par "mini-budget", while better than expected earnings from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of\par America\f28 \uc2 \f2  helped to boost risk appetite.\par     Investors are also focused on whether the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  falls to its weakest\par level against the dollar in 32 years.\par     Jeremy Hunt, who was appointed finance minister by Prime\par Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liz Truss\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Friday, reversed swathes of the 45-billion\par pound "mini-budget" that sparked market turmoil in which the\par pound hit record lows and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  was forced to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The pound has been the driver of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market this month\par so far, and the big change the \f28 \uc2 \f2 UK government\f28 \uc2 \f2  has announced has\par restored faith in the pound and taken the bid on the U.S. dollar\par out," said Adam Button, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at ForexLive.\par     British gilts rallied sharply after the news. Hunt replaced\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kwasi Kwarteng\f28 \uc2 \f2 , whose package of unfunded tax cuts on Sept. 23\par unleashed a bond market sell-off.\par     "For now, the market seems happy to give the new chancellor\par time and space to put the government's house back in order,"\par said Chris Beauchamp, chief market analyst at IG.\par     Sterling was last up 1.54% at $1.1348, after\par earlier reaching $1.1440, the highest since October 5.  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marc Chandler\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief market strategist at Bannockburn Global\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , says its likely that the pound bottomed at the record low\par of $1.0327 reached on September 26, which he called "an\par exaggeration."\par     The next major resistance level for the British \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par $1.15, he added.\par     Risk sentiment also improved after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported\par a smaller-than-expected drop in quarterly profit and said that\par its U.S. consumer client spending remained strong, even if it\par was slowing. \par     The dollar index against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par 0.82% to 112.11. It is holding just below a 20-year high of\par 114.78 hit on September 28.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's rapid interest rate increases have\par contributed to the strength of the dollar, but that may ease\par once the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reaches the point of pausing the\par hikes, \f28 \uc2 \f2 St. Louis Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 James Bullard\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Saturday.\par \par     The euro gained 1.19% against the greenback to\par $0.9838, the highest since October 6.\par     Traders are also on watch for any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the yen fell to a 32-year low of\par 148.97.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy the yen for the first\par time since 1998, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  stuck to its policy of\par maintaining ultra-low interest rates, which has battered the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year.\par     Japanese authorities kept up their warnings to the market on\par Monday of a firm response to overly rapid yen declines, after\par last week's fall and meetings of global financial leaders that\par acknowledged \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility.\par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 3:14PM (1914 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 112.1100       113.0500    -0.82%         17.193%       +113.2000   +111.9100\par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9838        $0.9723     +1.19%         -13.45%       +$0.9852    +$0.9715\par  Dollar/Yen                   148.9250       148.7850    +0.09%         +29.36%       +148.9550   +148.4000\par  Euro/Yen                     146.52         144.65      +1.29%         +12.