\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Pound rallies ahead of new finance minister's plans; yen wobbles\b0\par\par\uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2022\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout with comment, refreshes prices)\par \par \uc2 By Amanda Cooper\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 17 (Reuters) - The pound rallied on Monday as Britain's new finance minister prepared to unveil more fiscal plans aimed at soothing market volatility, while the Japanese yen was pinned near 32-year lows, with investors braced for any sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sterling rallied by as much as 1%, after Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  on Friday ditched a central plank of her government's "mini-budget" that sent the pound to record lows and put the bond market into free-fall, prompting multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  in the last couple of weeks.\par \par \uc2 Jeremy Hunt, who Truss appointed as finance minister after sacking \uc2 Kwasi Kwarteng\uc2  on Friday, has promised to restore Britain's economic credibility by fully accounting for the government's tax and spending plans, while insisting Truss remained in charge of the country.\par \par \uc2 British lawmakers will try to oust Truss this week despite Downing Street's warning that it could trigger a general election, the Daily Mail reported.\par \par \uc2 Investors are keeping a close eye on \uc2 UK government\uc2  bonds, which rallied in price sharply on Monday, thereby injecting a degree of confidence into the broader market.\par \par \uc2 "That was going to be the lightning rod. The fact that we've got yields drifting sharply lower this morning does suggest that at least up until now the measures that have been trialled and will be announced later have staunched some of the bleeding or the pessimism vis a vis the UK," CIBC Capital Markets head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy Jeremy Stretch said.\par \par \uc2 The pound was last up 0.7% against the dollar at $1.12460. It's regained almost 10% in value since hitting a record low of $1.0327 after the unveiling of the mini-budget, which contained around 45 billion pounds of unfunded tax cuts, on Sept. 23.\par \par \uc2 Yields on the 30-year gilt were down nearly 30 basis points at 4.5%, having veered above 5% at one point last week, forcing long-term investors such as pension funds to scramble for cash to protect their positions.\par \par \uc2 Hunt, a former foreign and health minister, will deliver a statement on the government's fiscal plans at 1000 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of England\uc2  on Friday concluded its emergency gilt market support.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the yen last bought 148.67 per dollar, not far off Friday's 32-year low of 148.86.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the yen for the first time since 1998, after the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  stuck to its policy of maintaining ultra-low interest rates, which has battered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities kept up their warnings to the market on Monday of a firm response to overly rapid yen declines, after last week's fall and meetings of global financial leaders that acknowledged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.\par \par \uc2 "We are not making the argument that there is a clear line in the sand at 150.00 for Japanese authorities - the whole idea of a 'line in the sand' in the current \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market appears unrealistic - but it\u8217\'20\'19s likely that allowing a move above 150.00 may well trigger an acceleration of the JPY sell-off which is exactly what Japan is trying to avoid," ING strategist \uc2 Francesco Pesole\uc2  said in a daily note.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the dollar was little changed on the day, trading around 113. The euro hovered at $0.9728, up 0.1%, while the Swiss franc gained 0.3% against the dollar to hold at 1.0025 francs, having hit parity on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Last week's red-hot U.S. inflation print has reinforced bets of another aggressive rate hike at the next FOMC meeting, with markets pricing in a 90.9% chance of a 75 basis point rate hike, and a 9.1% chance of a 100 bp increase.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index eased to 112.93.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Chinese offshore yuan last bought 7.2143 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 China's state banks stepped up their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend a weakening yuan on Monday, with banking sources telling Reuters these banks sold a high volume of U.S. dollars and used a combination of swaps and spot trades.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Rae Wee; Editing by Muralikumar Anantharaman and Ana Nicolaci da Costa) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-17T09:50:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221017eiah01d89\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
