\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 BOJ\uc2 's Wakatabe says yen's recent fluctuations too rapid, one-sided\b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2022\par 21:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wakatabe: No inconsistency in government, \uc2 BOJ\uc2  yen policies\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Must see some core inflation measures move to around 2%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will change policy when inflation sustainably at 2%\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 15 (Reuters) - \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Deputy Governor \uc2 Masazumi Wakatabe\uc2  said on Saturday the yen's recent fluctuations were "clearly too rapid and too one-sided," signalling caution over the potential economic damage from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slump to 32-year lows against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Wakatabe, speaking in a seminar during the \uc2 IMF\uc2  and \uc2 World Bank\uc2  annual meetings in Washington, also said Japan's government has made clear there was no discrepancy or inconsistency between its efforts to tame excessive yen declines, and the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's ultra-easy monetary policy aimed at achieving its 2% inflation target.\par \par \uc2 "Prime Minister (\uc2 Fumio) Kishida\uc2  supports the easy monetary policy to get out of a low inflationary environment," Wakatabe said when asked whether the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's ultra-low interest rate policy was driving down the yen, and contradicting the government's efforts to curb sharp yen falls through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He pointed to the Japanese leader's recent remarks to the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  that the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  needed to maintain its ultra-loose policy until wages went higher.\par \par \uc2 When asked about the yen's recent sharp declines, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  deputy governor said: "When it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations right now, it's clearly too rapid and too one-sided."\par \par \uc2 Under Japanese law, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 , has jurisdiction over exchange-rate policy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last month to arrest sharp yen drops, which were driven largely by the policy divergence between aggressive U.S. interest rate hikes and the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's resolve to keep monetary policy ultra-loose.\par \par \uc2 Wakatabe said the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  must maintain ultra-loose monetary policy because wage growth remains weak and inflation expectations, while rising, have yet to be firmly anchored around its 2% inflation target.\par \par \uc2 "We don't want to overshoot the target and undershoot the target. We'd like to have a stabilized 2% inflation rate down the road. That's when we are going to think about changing policy," Wakatabe said.\par \par \uc2 "I personally think... we have to see some core measures (of inflation) move around 2% and the distribution of price changes must be consistent with achieving our 2% target" to consider changing ultra-loose policy, he said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  remains an outlier among the world's central banks, many of which are tightening monetary policy to combat soaring inflation, as it focuses on underpinning a fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Japan's core consumer inflation accelerated to 2.8% in August, exceeding the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's 2% target for a fifth straight month as price pressures from raw materials and yen weakness broadened.\par \par \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\par \par \uc2 said in a separate seminar on Saturday that inflation will likely fall below 2% in the next fiscal year, and stressed the need to keep ultra-easy policy. (Reporting by Leika Kihara; Editing by Diane Craft and Paul Simao) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-15T20:39:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221015eiaf00v91\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
