\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rally pauses for breath after global stocks rebound\b0\par\par\uc2 798 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2022\par 07:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ankur Banerjee\par        SINGAPORE, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped on\par Friday as risk appetite returned to global stock markets and\par investors appeared to shift their focus away from U.S. interest\par rate considerations, even as red-hot  inflation data suggested \par more policy tightening was likely.\par     Traders also remained on edge about prospect of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in the yen, which was hovering above three-decade lows.\par     The dollar index fell 0.275%, extending the overnight\par session's 0.5% decline as investors seemingly brushed off data\par that showed U.S. consumer prices increased more than expected in\par September.\par     The dollar has been on a tear as soaring inflation,\par recession fears and worries over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies across\par the globe hit risk appetite.\par     But on Friday, Asian shares tailed Wall Street in moving\par higher.\par     Short-sellers in the stock market seemed to be driving the\par bounce in equities, which in turn pushed the dollar lower, said\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Singapore\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Moh Siong Sim.\par     "I think the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is taking its cue from the equity\par market," he said.\par     Despite this, the investment mood remained broadly cautious,\par which is likely to continue to support the dollar.\par     "I doubt the weaker dollar will sustain ... the dollar is\par the safe-haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  currently," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of\par Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Carol Kong said.\par     Analysts also pointed to Thursday reports of a possible\par U-turn by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 UK government\f28 \uc2 \f2  on its fiscal plans, which also\par supported risk sentiment.\par     Sterling made steep gains overnight against the\par dollar as a result. It was last trading at $1.1311, down 0.15%\par on the day.\par     British finance minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kwasi Kwarteng\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut short his trip\par to Washington amid reports that Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liz Truss\f28 \uc2 \f2  was\par considering reversing elements of the plan announced three weeks\par ago that triggered turmoil in financial markets.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  has had to step in to restore calm,\par announcing an emergency bond buying programme but is also\par adamant it will end the programme on Friday.\par     Focus now shifts to next month's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  policy\par meeting where it is expected to deliver another 75-basis-point\par rate increase. Futures prices also reflect about a one-in-10\par chance of a full percentage-point rate hike next month.     \par     Elsewhere, the dollar was trading at 147.33 to the yen\par , below the 32-year peak of 147.665 it hit in the\par previous session.\par     Investors remained on watch for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the\par Japanese government to prop up the fragile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Finance\par Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  reiterated the government's readiness\par to take "appropriate action" against excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par volatility.\par     "Given the overnight CPI (consumer price index) shock and\par the fact that some economists are increasing their expectations\par for Fed hikes, the yen's relative stability is especially\par impressive," \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Vail\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief global strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nikko Asset\par Management\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tokyo. "MOF's efforts, therefore, have been\par successful."\par     Last month, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy yen for the first time\par since 1998, in an attempt to shore up the battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "There is still a risk of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  just on the back\par of on how weak the yen is," Kong said, but cautioned that any\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely to be successful. \par     The Australian dollar was up 0.56% versus the\par greenback at $0.633, coming off a two and half year low it\par touched in the previous session. The kiwi was up 0.71%\par at $0.567 and was set for its first weekly gains in nine weeks. \par    \par     The euro nudged up 0.06% to $0.9779\par ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0430 GMT\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct     High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                 \par                                               Session                                           \par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9779        $0.9778     +0.02%         -13.98%     +0.9808     +0.9763\par  Dollar/Yen                   147.4450       147.3100    +0.03%         +28.11%     +147.4550   +147.2500\par  Euro/Yen         <EURJPY=EB  144.20         143.95      +0.17%         +10.65%     +144.3400   +143.8400\par                   S>                                                                  