 risk of a drop is amplified by the betting on a rise USD/JPY gears up for fresh 24-year highs, Japan issues \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY hit a new 24-year high at 146.98, on Wed, according to EBS data \u8226\'20\'22 Spot consolidating below 146.98, Thursday has seen a 146.68-91 range so far \u8226\'20\'22 Japan's Fin Min warns of 'decisive' action vs rapid yen falls \u8226\'20\'22 Remains above 145.90 level that prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY chart shows a market ripe for new multi-year highs \u8226\'20\'22 Dollar typically climbs against the yen in October \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY's log correlation with USD/JPY is high, 60-day measure above +0.50 GBP/USD rises to two-day top as long-dated gilt yields fall \u8226\'20\'22 Cable ascends to 1.1153 (two-day high) as long-dated gilt yields fall \u8226\'20\'22 1.1061 was early London intra-day low \u8226\'20\'22 Offers may emerge near 1.1180 and 1.12 if GBP/USD extends north \u8226\'20\'22 1.1180 was Tuesday's top (before Bailey-spurred drop to 1.0925 two-week low) \u8226\'20\'22 UK minister shies away from committing to corporate tax plan \u8226\'20\'22 U.S. Sept inflation data due 1230 GMT; CPI f/c 8.1% YY, core CPI f/c 6.5% YY AUD/USD up to threaten 0.63 before U.S. inflation data \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD eyes 0.63 after rising from 0.6265 (intra-day low at 0706 GMT) \u8226\'20\'22 Offers just shy of 0.63 capped rally from Wednesday's 30-month low of 0.6236 \u8226\'20\'22 Rally towards 0.63 aided by European stocks turning positive \u8226\'20\'22 More offers expected ahead of 0.6350 (0.6346 was Tuesday's high) \u8226\'20\'22 U.S. Sept inflation data due 1230 GMT; CPI f/c 8.1% YY; core CPI f/c 6.5% \u8226\'20\'22 Money markets currently see 90% chance of 75 bps Fed hike Nov 2 Pound shouldn't be greatly affected by bond turmoil The pound shouldn't be directly affected by UK bond turmoil, which is being driven mainly by British pension firms and does not involve \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions, so has no direct impact for sterling.That said, such big market shifts in such a short time frame and their destabilizing effect for some core UK asset markets do have potential to spur risk averse trading behavior by foreign firms, which supports safe \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like dollar and Swiss franc and could pressure the pound. An alternative is that foreign companies use this opportunity to prosper from an adjustment that is being forced upon UK firms, lifting yields to levels that may prove unsustainable. Times when companies are forced to act without much consideration for the price are often the points when others are able to make money. There is a good chance of a sizable adjustment once normal conditions return once those forced to act have completed their interest. Should foreign firms buy into the distressed selling of UK bonds, the pound could draw support. What really matters for GBP/USD traders is the pair's break lower out of long-term trading ranges. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3Vs0yjk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  Dollar has plenty more upside as rivals remain at risk The U.S. dollar could make big gains in the days and weeks ahead as its major rivals look set to suffer further losses. The USD index continues to trade well above the 109.144 Fibo, a 76.4% retrace of the 121.020 to 70.698 (2001-2008) drop, increasing the odds for much bigger gains. Also 14-week momentum remains positive. The dollar's fate is especially pinned to the biggest components of the index, the euro and yen. EUR/USD's has registered three daily closes under the 0.9708 Fibo, a 61.8% retrace of the 0.9528 to 0.9999 (September to October) rise, on Monday and Tuesday and Wednesday. That could spark a much bigger EUR/USD collapse in coming sessions. Japan is ready to take "decisive" action against rapid yen declines, Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said. However, yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems futile as the chasm between the Federal Reserve and Bank of Japan has continued to widen. There is scope for USD/JPY to break above the 1998 147.64 (EBS) peak. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3TcLNi4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-16T11:00:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221013eiad01s75\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
